    mslm:evidenceJson "{\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"compartment\": [{\"accession\": \"0005789\", \"className\": \"Compartment\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 12045, \"definition\": \"The lipid bilayer surrounding the endoplasmic reticulum.\", \"displayName\": \"endoplasmic reticulum membrane\", \"name\": \"endoplasmic reticulum membrane\", \"schemaClass\": \"Compartment\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0005789\"}, {\"accession\": \"0005743\", \"className\": \"Compartment\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 70616, \"definition\": \"The inner, i.e. lumen-facing, lipid bilayer of the mitochondrial envelope. It is highly folded to form cristae.\", \"displayName\": \"mitochondrial inner membrane\", \"name\": \"mitochondrial inner membrane\", \"schemaClass\": \"Compartment\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0005743\"}], \"crossReference\": [{\"className\": \"DatabaseIdentifier\", \"databaseName\": \"RHEA\", \"dbId\": 12689776, \"displayName\": \"RHEA:38695\", \"identifier\": \"38695\", \"schemaClass\": \"DatabaseIdentifier\", \"url\": \"https://www.rhea-db.org/rhea/38695\"}], \"dbId\": 1482857, \"displayName\": \"CL transports from the ER to the IM\", \"followingEvent\": [1482778], \"goBiologicalProcess\": {\"accession\": \"0015914\", \"className\": \"GO_BiologicalProcess\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 21991, \"definition\": \"The directed movement of phospholipids into, out of or within a cell, or between cells, by means of some agent such as a transporter or pore. Phospholipids are any lipids containing phosphoric acid as a mono- or diester.\", \"displayName\": \"phospholipid transport\", \"name\": \"phospholipid transport\", \"schemaClass\": \"GO_BiologicalProcess\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0015914\"}, \"input\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"consumedByEvent\": [1482857], \"dbId\": 1524081, \"displayName\": \"CL [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"