\": \"Evidence that phosphatidylserine is imported into mitochondria via a mitochondria-associated membrane and that the majority of mitochondrial phosphatidylethanolamine is derived from decarboxylation of phosphatidylserine\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7744750\", \"volume\": 270, \"year\": 1995}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1482820, \"displayName\": \"Characterization of a microsomal subfraction associated with mitochondria of the yeast, Saccharomyces cerevisiae. Involvement in synthesis and import of phospholipids into mitochondria\", \"journal\": \"Biochim Biophys Acta\", \"pages\": \"214-20\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 7696296, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Characterization of a microsomal subfraction associated with mitochondria of the yeast, Saccharomyces cerevisiae. Involvement in synthesis and import of phospholipids into mitochondria\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7696296\", \"volume\": 1234, \"year\": 1995}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1482853, \"displayName\": \"Involvement of mitochondrial contact sites in the subcellular compartmentalization of phospholipid biosynthetic enzymes\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"25985-92\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 8245031, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Involvement of mitochondrial contact sites in the subcellular compartmentalization of phospholipid biosynthetic enzymes\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8245031\", \"volume\": 268, \"year\": 1993}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1482865, \"displayName\": \"Phospholipid synthesis in a membrane fraction associated with mitochondria\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"7248-56\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 2332429, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Phospholipid synthesis in a membrane fraction associated with mitochondria\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2332429\", \"volume\": 265, \"year\": 1990}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1482804, \"displayName\": \"Making heads or tails of phospholipids in mitochondria\", \"journal\": \"J Cell Biol\", \"pages\": \"7-16\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 21220505, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Making heads or tails of phospholipids in mitochondria\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21220505\", \"volume\": 192, \"year\": 2011}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CL transports from the ER to the IM\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1524072, \"displayName\": \"cardiolipin [mitochondrial inner membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"cardiolipin\", \"CL\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1482857], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1524072\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1524072.3\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1482861, \"displayName\": \"MLCL is acylated to CL by LCLAT1 (ER)\", \"followingEvent\": [1482857], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"MLCL is acylated to CL by LCLAT1 (ER)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482861\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482861.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482857\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482857.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1482913, \"displayName\": \"Cardiolipin (CL) transports via membrane contact sites betwe...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Cardiolipin (CL) transports via membrane contact sites between the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) and the inner mitochondria membranes (IM) (Osman et al. 2011, Vance 1990, Gaigg et al. 1995, Zhao et al. 2009, Simbeni et al. 1991, Ardail et al. 1993, Shiao et al., 1995).\"}]}" ;
