1498738.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1524021, \"displayName\": \"LCFA(-) [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"LCFA(-)\", \"long-chain fatty acid anion\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1482884], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1524021\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1524021.3\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1483077, \"displayName\": \"PE transports from the mitochondrial membrane to the ER\", \"followingEvent\": [1482884], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PE transports from the mitochondrial membrane to the ER\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1483077\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1483077.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1482667, \"displayName\": \"1-acyl LPE is acylated to PE by LPEAT\", \"followingEvent\": [1482884], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"1-acyl LPE is acylated to PE by LPEAT\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482667\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482667.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1482646, \"displayName\": \"2-acyl LPE is acylated to PE by LPEAT\", \"followingEvent\": [1482884], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"2-acyl LPE is acylated to PE by LPEAT\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482646\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482646.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1482962, \"displayName\": \"CDP-ETA and DAG are converted to PE by CEPT1/EPT1\", \"followingEvent\": [1482884], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CDP-ETA and DAG are converted to PE by CEPT1/EPT1\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482962\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482962.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482884\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482884.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1482858, \"displayName\": \"At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidyletha...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidylethanolamine (PE) is hydrolyzed, and has one of its acyl chains cleaved off, by phospholipase A2 to form 1-acyl lysophosphatidylethanolamine (LPE).    The phospholipases are either cytosolic phospholipase A2 alpha/beta/delta/epsilon/zeta (PLA2G(4A/B/D/E/F) (Ghosh et al. 2006, Yamashita et al. 2009, Yamashita et al. 1999, Ghomashchi et al. 2010), 85 kDa calcium-independent phospholipase A2 (PLA2G6) (Larsson et al. 1998, Ma et al. 1999, Larsson Forsell et al. 1999), group XVI phospholipase A2 (PLA2G16)  (Duncan et al. 2008), or Phospholipase B-like 1 (PLBD1) (Xu et al. 2009).  PLBD1 acts as a phospholipase A2 but in addition has the propensity to hydrolyze the lysophospholipid formed in its initial reaction.\"}]}" ;
