lglycerol\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1483121], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-426955\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-426955.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 111294, \"displayName\": \"PPi [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PPi\", \"diphosphate(3-)\", \"pyrophosphate\", \"diphosphoric acid\", \"pyrophosphoric acid\", \"diphosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1483121], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-111294\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-111294.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 75885, \"displayName\": \"1-acyl LPA is acylated to PA by AGPAT (LPAAT)\", \"followingEvent\": [1483121], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"1-acyl LPA is acylated to PA by AGPAT (LPAAT)\", \"1-acyl-glycerol 3-phosphate + acyl-CoA => 1,2-diacyl-glycerol 3-phosphate + CoASH\", \"lysophosphatidic acid + fatty acyl CoA  => phosphatidic acid + CoA (1) \"], \"releaseDate\": \"2004-07-06\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-75885\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-75885.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1483182, \"displayName\": \"PC is hydrolyzed to PA and choline by PLD1/2\", \"followingEvent\": [1483121], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PC is hydrolyzed to PA and choline by PLD1/2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1483182\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1483182.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1483121\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1483121.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1482945, \"displayName\": \"At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidate cy...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"At the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) membrane, phosphatidate cytidylyltransferase 1 (CDS1) converts phosphatidic acid (PA) and cytidine triphosphate (CTP) into cytidine diphosphate-diacylglycerol (CDP-DAG).  Both ER and mitochondrial membranes have the capability to synthesize cytidine diphosphate-diacylglycerol (CDP-DAG) with phosphatidate cytidylyltransferase 1 and 2 (CDS1 and CDS2) (Lykidis et al. 1997).  However, transport of CDP-DAG between organelles cannot be ruled out (Stuhne-Sekalec et al. 1986).\"}]}" ;
