    mslm:evidenceJson "{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"compartment\": [{\"accession\": \"0005789\", \"className\": \"Compartment\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 12045, \"definition\": \"The lipid bilayer surrounding the endoplasmic reticulum.\", \"displayName\": \"endoplasmic reticulum membrane\", \"name\": \"endoplasmic reticulum membrane\", \"schemaClass\": \"Compartment\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0005789\"}, {\"accession\": \"0031902\", \"className\": \"Compartment\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 172574, \"definition\": \"The lipid bilayer surrounding a late endosome.\", \"displayName\": \"late endosome membrane\", \"name\": \"late endosome membrane\", \"schemaClass\": \"Compartment\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0031902\"}], \"crossReference\": [{\"className\": \"DatabaseIdentifier\", \"databaseName\": \"RHEA\", \"dbId\": 12690733, \"displayName\": \"RHEA:39743\", \"identifier\": \"39743\", \"schemaClass\": \"DatabaseIdentifier\", \"url\": \"https://www.rhea-db.org/rhea/39743\"}], \"dbId\": 1483218, \"displayName\": \"PG transports from the ER membrane to the late endosome membrane\", \"input\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"consumedByEvent\": [1483218], \"dbId\": 1483256, \"displayName\": \"PG [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PG\", \"1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1'-sn-glycerol)(1-)\", \"phosphatidylglycerol\"], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1483256\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1483256.4\"}], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"literatureReference\": [{\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1483042, \"displayName\": \"De novo biosynthesis of the late endosome lipid, bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate\", \"journal\": \"J Lipid Res\", \"pages\": \"1997-2008\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 17558022, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"De novo biosynthesis of the late endosome lipid, bis(monoacylglycero)phosphate\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17558022\", \"volume\": 48, \"year\": 2007}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1482582, \"displayName\": \"A lipid associated with the antiphospholipid syndrome regulates endosome structure and function\", \"journal\": \"Nature\", \"pages\": \"193-7\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 9515966, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"A lipid associated with the antiphospholipid syndrome regulates endosome structure and function\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9515966\", \"volume\": 392, \"year\": 1998}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1483140, \"displayName\": \"Late endosomal membranes rich in lysobisphosphatidic acid regulate cholesterol transport\", \"journal\": \"Nat Cell Biol\", \"pages\": \"113-8\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 10559883, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Late endosomal membranes rich in lysobisphosphatidic acid regulate cholesterol transport\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10559883\", \"volume\": 1, \"year\": 1999}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1483097, \"displayName\": \"Short-range intracellular trafficking of small molecules across endoplasmic reticulum junctions\", \"journal\": \"Trends Cell Biol\", \"pages\": \"483-90\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 15350976, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Short-range intracellular trafficking of small molecules across endoplasmic reticulum junctions\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/15350976\", \"volume\": 14, \"year\": 2004}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1483102, \"displayName\": \"Membrane contacts between endosomes and ER provide sites for PTP1B-epidermal growth factor receptor interaction\", \"journal\": \"Nat Cell Biol\", \"pages\": \"267-72\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 20118922, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Membrane contacts between endosomes and ER provide sites for PTP1B-epidermal growth factor receptor interaction\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20118922\", \"volume\": 12, \"year\": 2010}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PG transports from the ER membrane to the late endosome membrane\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1524139, \"displayName\": \"PG [late endosome membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PG\", \"1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1'-sn-glycerol)(1-)\", \"phosphatidylglycerol\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1483218], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1524139\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1524139.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1483142, \"displayName\": \"PC is transphosphatidylated to PG by PLD1-4/6\", \"followingEvent\": [1483218], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PC is transphosphatidylated to PG by PLD1-4/6\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1483142\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1483142.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1482539, \"displayName\": \"1-acyl LPG is acylated to PG by LPGAT\", \"followingEvent\": [1483218], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"1-acyl LPG is acylated to PG by LPGAT\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482539\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482539.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1482635, \"displayName\": \"2-acyl LPG is acylated to PG by LPGAT\", \"followingEvent\": [1483218], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"2-acyl LPG is acylated to PG by LPGAT\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482635\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482635.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1483218\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1483218.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1483128, \"displayName\": \"Lysobisphosphatidic acid, also known as bis(monoacylglycerol...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Lysobisphosphatidic acid, also known as bis(monoacylglycerol) hydrogen phosphate (BMP), is enriched in late endosomes and not found in the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) or mitochondria where phosphatidylglycerol (PG) is synthesised.  Late endosomes form membrane contact sites with the ER, providing a means for PG to enter the late endosome and be converted to BMP (Levine 2004, Eden et al. 2010, Kobayashi et al. 1998, Hullin-Matsuda et al. 2007, Kobayashi et al. 1999).\"}]}" ;
