: \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1483222\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1483222.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1483119, \"displayName\": \"In the cytosol, ethanolamine (ETA) is phosphorylated to phos...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"In the cytosol, ethanolamine (ETA) is phosphorylated to phosphoethanolamine (PETA) by choline kinase (CHK) dimer or by ethanolamine kinase 1/2 (ETNK1/2) (Lykidis et al. 2001, Gallego-Ortega et al. 2009).  CHK dimer consists of either choline kinase alpha subunit (CHKA) or beta subunit (CHKB) homodimer, or of CHKA:CHKB heterodimer.\"}]}" ;
