\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 29747811, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Ganglioside Metabolism in Health and Disease\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/29747811\", \"volume\": 156, \"year\": 2018}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9840312, \"displayName\": \"Emerging concepts of ganglioside metabolism\", \"journal\": \"FEBS Lett\", \"pages\": \"3835-3864\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 29802621, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Emerging concepts of ganglioside metabolism\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/29802621\", \"volume\": 592, \"year\": 2018}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9840850, \"displayName\": \"Purification and characterization of beta-N-acetylhexosaminidase I from human placenta\", \"journal\": \"J Biochem\", \"pages\": \"827-31\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 2976757, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Purification and characterization of beta-N-acetylhexosaminidase I from human placenta\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2976757\", \"volume\": 104, \"year\": 1988}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9840817, \"displayName\": \"Prosaposin deficiency: further characterization of the sphingolipid activator protein-deficient sibs. Multiple glycolipid elevations (including lactosylceramidosis), partial enzyme deficiencies and ultrastructure of the skin in this generalized sphingolipid storage disease\", \"journal\": \"Hum Genet\", \"pages\": \"143-52\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 8370580, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Prosaposin deficiency: further characterization of the sphingolipid activator protein-deficient sibs. Multiple glycolipid elevations (including lactosylceramidosis), partial enzyme deficiencies and ultrastructure of the skin in this generalized sphingolipid storage disease\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8370580\", \"volume\": 92, \"year\": 1993}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10276267, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\", \"inferredFrom\": [1605632], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-1605632.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 11025190, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\", \"inferredFrom\": [1605632], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Dictyostelium discoideum\", \"stId\": \"R-DDI-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DDI-1605632.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10958362, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\", \"inferredFrom\": [1605632], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-1605632.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10780816, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\", \"inferredFrom\": [1605632], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Gallus gallus\", \"stId\": \"R-GGA-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-GGA-1605632.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10500870, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\", \"inferredFrom\": [1605632], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-1605632.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10386304, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\", \"inferredFrom\": [1605632], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-1605632.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10162926, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\", \"inferredFrom\": [1605632], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-1605632.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10040764, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\", \"inferredFrom\": [1605632], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):Gb4Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-1605632.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1605658, \"displayName\": \"GalNAc [lysosomal lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"GalNAc\", \"N-acetyl-D-galactosamine\", \"N-acetylgalactosamine\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1605632], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1605658\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1605658.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 9840848, \"displayName\": \"PSAP(195-273):Gb3Cer:PE [lysosomal lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 3, \"name\": [\"PSAP(195-273):Gb3Cer:PE\", \"mobilized Gb3Cer\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1605632], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9840848\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840848.1\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9840470, \"displayName\": \"PSAP(195-273) dimer:PE binds and mobilizes ligands\", \"followingEvent\": [1605632], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PSAP(195-273) dimer:PE binds and mobilizes ligands\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2023-09-13\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9840470\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840470.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2011-12-06\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1605632\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1605632.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1660668, \"displayName\": \"The globotetraosylceramide Gb4Cer (Gb4) is cleaved by both b...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"The globotetraosylceramide Gb4Cer (Gb4) is cleaved by both beta-hexosaminidase complexes bHEXA and bHEXB to form Gb3Cer (Kinoshita et al. 1988; Mark et al. 2003). Gb4Cer is present at elevated levels in nerve cells in Sandhoff disease (Tay-Sachs disease variant O, MIM: 268800), a hexosaminidase beta subunit (HEXB) deficiency, which leads to low levels of both bHEX complexes bHEXA and bHEXB (Sandhoff et al., 1971; reviewed in Sandhoff et al., 2018; Sandhoff & Sandhoff, 2018). There are three forms of hexosaminidase complexes: hexosaminidase A, B and S. The A form is a tetramer of the subunits alpha (HEXA, beta A) and beta (HEXB, beta B) dimers. The B form is a tetramer of two beta subunit dimers, and the S form a tetramer of two HEXA dimers (O'Dowd et al. 1988, Mahuran et al. 1988). Both bHEXA and bHEXB can cleave GalNAc from globosides (glycosphingolipids based on the Gb3Cer structure, with sugars added to the Gal-Gal-Glu side chain).<br>Researchers observed elevated Gb4Cer in prosaposin deficiency (PSAPD, MIM: 611721) cases, a rare disease with low levels of all saposins. We have curated Saposin B (PSAP(195-273)) as essential cofactor to the reaction (Bradova et al., 1993).\"}]}" ;
