NEU1,4 hydrolyze PSAP(195-273):GM3:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2011-12-06\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1605724\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1605724.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1605736, \"displayName\": \"GLA hydrolyzes PSAP(195-273):Gb3Cer:PE\", \"followingEvent\": [1606312], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"GLA hydrolyzes PSAP(195-273):Gb3Cer:PE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2011-12-06\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1605736\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1605736.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9840949, \"displayName\": \"ARSA removes sulfate from SM3\", \"followingEvent\": [1606312], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ARSA removes sulfate from SM3\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2023-09-13\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9840949\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840949.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9840833, \"displayName\": \"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze GM2A:GA2 to GM2A:LacCer\", \"followingEvent\": [1606312], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"bHEXA,bHEXB hydrolyze GM2A:GA2 to GM2A:LacCer\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2023-09-13\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9840833\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840833.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2011-12-06\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1606312\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1606312.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1606313, \"displayName\": \"Lactosylceramide (LacCer) is the central intermediate in gly...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Lactosylceramide (LacCer) is the central intermediate in glycosphingolipid catabolism. Beta-galactosidase (GLB1) cleaves the galactose moiety from LacCer to form glucosylceramide. LacCer accumulates in GLB1 deficiencies (MIM: 611458) like GM1-gangliosidosis but also in prosaposin deficiency (PSAPD, MIM: 611721), which shows saposin cofactors are essential for the reaction (Asp et al. 1969; Bradova et al., 1993). We follow Sandhoff & Sandhoff (2018), who state that Saposins B/C bind to LacCer.\"}]}" ;
