 \"The evolutionary conservation of a novel protein modification, the conversion of cysteine to serinesemialdehyde in arylsulfatase from Volvox carteri\", \"journal\": \"Eur J Biochem\", \"pages\": \"341-5\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 8681943, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"The evolutionary conservation of a novel protein modification, the conversion of cysteine to serinesemialdehyde in arylsulfatase from Volvox carteri\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8681943\", \"volume\": 238, \"year\": 1996}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1614341, \"displayName\": \"A novel protein modification generating an aldehyde group in sulfatases: its role in catalysis and disease\", \"journal\": \"Bioessays\", \"pages\": \"505-10\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 9699462, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"A novel protein modification generating an aldehyde group in sulfatases: its role in catalysis and disease\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9699462\", \"volume\": 20, \"year\": 1998}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1663155, \"displayName\": \"A general binding mechanism for all human sulfatases by the formylglycine-generating enzyme\", \"journal\": \"Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A\", \"pages\": \"81-6\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 16368756, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"A general binding mechanism for all human sulfatases by the formylglycine-generating enzyme\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16368756\", \"volume\": 103, \"year\": 2006}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SUMF1 mediates the oxidation of cysteine to formylglycine, producing active arylsulfatases\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10871396, \"displayName\": \"SUMF1 mediates the oxidation of cysteine to formylglycine, producing active arylsulfatases\", \"inferredFrom\": [1614362], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDe