 + Na+ [extracellular] -> carnitine [cytosol] + Na+ [cytosol]\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-165026\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-165026.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10243888, \"displayName\": \"OCTN2 / SLC22A5 transports CAR from extracellular space to cytosol\", \"inferredFrom\": [165026], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"OCTN2 / SLC22A5 transports CAR from extracellular space to cytosol\", \"(R)-carnitine(out) + Na(+)(out) = (R)-carnitine(in) + Na(+)(in)\", \"carnitine [extracellular] + Na+ [extracellular] -> carnitine [cytosol] + Na+ [cytosol]\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-165026\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-165026.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10122537, \"displayName\": \"OCTN2 / SLC22A5 transports CAR from extracellular space to cytosol\", \"inferredFrom\": [165026], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"OCTN2 / SLC22A5 transports CAR from extracellular space to cytosol\", \"(R)-carnitine(out) + Na(+)(out) = (R)-carnitine(in) + Na(+)(in)\", \"carnitine [extracellular] + Na+ [extracellular] -> carnitine [cytosol] + Na+ [cytosol]\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-165026\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-165026.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10002038, \"displayName\": \"OCTN2 / SLC22A5 transports CAR from extracellular space to cytosol\", \"inferredFrom\": [165026], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"OCTN2 / SLC22A5 transports CAR from extracellular space to cytosol\", \"(R)-carnitine(out) + Na(+)(out) = (R)-carnitine(in) + Na(+)(in)\", \"carnitine [extracellular] + Na+ [extracellular] -> carnitine [cytosol] + Na+ [cytosol]\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-165026\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-165026.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 30235, \"displayName\": \"CAR [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CAR\", \"(R)-carnitine\", \"gamma-Trimethyl-hydroxybutyrobetaine\", \"carnitine\", \"3-Hydroxy-4-trimethylammoniobutanoate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [165026], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-30235\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-30235.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 83910, \"displayName\": \"Na+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Na+\", \"sodium(1+)\", \"sodium ion\", \"Sodium\"], \"producedByEvent\": [165026], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-83910\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-83910.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"uncertain\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 164967, \"displayName\": \"Unknown carnitine exporter transports CAR from the cytosol to the extracellular space\", \"followingEvent\": [165026], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Unknown carnitine exporter transports CAR from the cytosol to the extracellular space\", \"carnitine [cytosol] -> carnitine [extracellular]\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2017-03-27\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-164967\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-164967.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2017-03-27\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-165026\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-165026.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 164978, \"displayName\": \"OCTN2 (organic cation transporter novel 2, encoded by the SL...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"OCTN2 (organic cation transporter novel 2, encoded by the SLC22A5 gene) mediates the sodium-dependent transport of CAR (carnitine) from the extracellular space into the cytosol.<p>While humans are capable of synthesizing carnitine de novo, the enzyme that catalyzes the last reaction of the biosynthetic pathway is found only in liver and kidney cells, and at very low levels in brain cells. Other tissues that require carnitine, such as muscle, are dependent on transport systems that mediate its export from the liver and uptake by other tissues (Kerner & Hoppel 1998). The specific transport systems responsible for liver export have been characterized biochemically in model organisms but specific transport proteins have not yet been identified. OCTN2 is the major transporter responsible for carnitine uptake in extrahepatic tissues, as demonstrated both by the biochemical characterization of overexpressed recombinant human protein (Tamai et al. 1998) and by the appearance of symptoms of carnitine deficiency in humans lacking a functional SLC22A5 gene (Seth et al. 1999; reviewed by Longo et al. 2016).\"}]}" ;
