osome membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI\", \"1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol(1-)\", \"Phosphatidyl 1D-myo-inositol\", \"1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol\"], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1806195\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1806195.4\"}], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"literatureReference\": [{\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1675955, \"displayName\": \"PIKfyve, a mammalian ortholog of yeast Fab1p lipid kinase, synthesizes 5-phosphoinositides. Effect of insulin\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"21589-97\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 10419465, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"PIKfyve, a mammalian ortholog of yeast Fab1p lipid kinase, synthesizes 5-phosphoinositides. Effect of insulin\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10419465\", \"volume\": 274, \"year\": 1999}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1460290, \"displayName\": \"Phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate biosynthesis is linked to PIKfyve and is involved in osmotic response pathway in mammalian cells\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"47276-84\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 12270933, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate biosynthesis is linked to PIKfyve and is involved in osmotic response pathway in mammalian cells\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12270933\", \"volume\": 277, \"year\": 2002}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI is phosphorylated to PI5P by PIKFYVE at the late endosome membrane\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29370, \"displayName\": \"ADP [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ADP\", \"ADP(3-)\", \"Adenosine 5'-diphosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1675866], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29370\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29370.6\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1806212, \"displayName\": \"PI5P [late endosome membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI5P\", \"1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 5-phosphate(3-)\", \"1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 5-phosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1675866], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1806212\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1806212.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1675795, \"displayName\": \"PI3P is dephosphorylated to PI by MTM proteins at the late endosome membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1675866], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI3P is dephosphorylated to PI by MTM proteins at the late endosome membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675795\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675795.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675866\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675866.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1675826, \"displayName\": \"At the late endosome membrane, the PAS complex, consisting o...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"At the late endosome membrane, the PAS complex, consisting of FYVE finger-containing phosphoinositide kinase (PIKFYVE), yeast VAC14 homologue (VAC14), and polyphosphoinositide phosphatase aka SAC3 (FIG4), binds to the membrane via PIKFYVE's FYVE finger.  The PIKFYVE kinase component phosphorylates phosphatidylinositol (PI) to phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate (PI5P) (Sbrissa et al. 1999, Sbrissa et al. 2002).  The PAS complex is present in the cytosol and is recruited to the membrane.\"}]}" ;
