878-91\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 17556371, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Core protein machinery for mammalian phosphatidylinositol 3,5-bisphosphate synthesis and turnover that regulates the progression of endosomal transport. Novel Sac phosphatase joins the ArPIKfyve-PIKfyve complex\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/17556371\", \"volume\": 282, \"year\": 2007}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1460276, \"displayName\": \"ArPIKfyve homomeric and heteromeric interactions scaffold PIKfyve and Sac3 in a complex to promote PIKfyve activity and functionality\", \"journal\": \"J Mol Biol\", \"pages\": \"766-79\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 18950639, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"ArPIKfyve homomeric and heteromeric interactions scaffold PIKfyve and Sac3 in a complex to promote PIKfyve activity and functionality\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18950639\", \"volume\": 384, \"year\": 2008}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1676068, \"displayName\": \"Phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate-interacting domains in PIKfyve. Binding specificity and role in PIKfyve. Endomenbrane localization\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"6073-9\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 11706043, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate-interacting domains in PIKfyve. Binding specificity and role in PIKfyve. Endomenbrane localization\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11706043\", \"volume\": 277, \"year\": 2002}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI3P is phosphorylated to PI(3,5)P2 by PIKFYVE at the Golgi membrane\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29370, \"displayName\": \"ADP [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ADP\", \"ADP(3-)\", \"Adenosine 5'-diphosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1675921], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29370\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29370.6\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1806290, \"displayName\": \"PI(3,5)P2 [Golgi membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI(3,5)P2\", \"1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,5-bisphosphate(5-)\", \"1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,5-bisphosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1675921], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1806290\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1806290.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1675961, \"displayName\": \"PI is phosphorylated to PI3P by PIK3C2A/3 at the Golgi membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1675921], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI is phosphorylated to PI3P by PIK3C2A/3 at the Golgi membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675961\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675961.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1676005, \"displayName\": \"PI(3,5)P2 is dephosphorylated to PI3P by FIG4 at the Golgi membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1675921], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI(3,5)P2 is dephosphorylated to PI3P by FIG4 at the Golgi membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676005\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676005.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675921\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675921.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1675926, \"displayName\": \"At the Golgi membrane, the PAS complex, consisting of FYVE f...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"At the Golgi membrane, the PAS complex, consisting of FYVE finger-containing phosphoinositide kinase (PIKFYVE), yeast VAC14 homologue (VAC14), and polyphosphoinositide phosphatase aka SAC3 (FIG4), binds to the membrane via PIKFYVE's FYVE finger (Sbrissa et al. 2002).  The PIKFYVE kinase component phosphorylates phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate (PI3P) to phosphatidylinositol 3,5-bisphosphate PI(3,5)P2 (Sbrissa et al. 1999, McEwen et al. 1999).  The PAS complex is present in the cytosol and is recruited to the membrane (Sbrissa et al. 2007). VAC14 acts as a scaffolding protein via its C-terminal domain (Sbrissa et al. 2008).\"}]}" ;
