)P2 is phosphorylated to PI(3,4,5)P3 by PIK3C[1] at the plasma membrane\", \"inferredFrom\": [1676048], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI(4,5)P2 is phosphorylated to PI(3,4,5)P3 by PIK3C[1] at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-1676048\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-1676048.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 179838, \"displayName\": \"PI(3,4,5)P3 [plasma membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI(3,4,5)P3\", \"1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate(7-)\", \"PIP3\", \"1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate\", \"Phosphatidylinositol-3,4,5-trisphosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1676048], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-179838\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-179838.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29370, \"displayName\": \"ADP [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ADP\", \"ADP(3-)\", \"Adenosine 5'-diphosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [1676048], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29370\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29370.6\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1676082, \"displayName\": \"PI4P is phosphorylated to PI(4,5)P2 by PIP5K1A-C at the plasma membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1676048], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI4P is phosphorylated to PI(4,5)P2 by PIP5K1A-C at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676082\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676082.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 199456, \"displayName\": \"PTEN dephosphorylates PIP3\", \"followingEvent\": [1676048], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PTEN dephosphorylates PIP3\", \"PI(3,4,5)P3 is dephosphorylated to PI (4,5)P2 by PTEN at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-03-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-199456\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-199456.5\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1675776, \"displayName\": \"PI5P is phosphorylated to PI(4,5)P2 by PIP4K2 dimers at the plasma membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1676048], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI5P is phosphorylated to PI(4,5)P2 by PIP4K2 dimers at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675776\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675776.5\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676048\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676048.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1675804, \"displayName\": \"At the plasma membrane, phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphat...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"At the plasma membrane, phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate 3-kinase catalytic subunits form complexes with regulatory subunits.  These complexes phosphorylate phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate (PI(4,5)P2) to phosphatidylinositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate (PI(3,4,5)P3) (Stephens et al. 1997).  The PI(4,5)P2 3-kinase complexes involved are: PI(4,5)P2 3-kinase catalytic subunit alpha isoform (PIK3CA) bound to PI 3-kinase regulatory subunit alpha/beta/gamma (PIK3R1/2/3); beta (PIK3CB) bound to PIK3R1/2/3; delta (PIK3CD) bound to PIK3R1/2/3; and gamma (PIK3CG) bound to PI 3-kinase regulatory subunit 5 (PIK3R5) or 6 (PIK3R6).<br><br>The following lists the above proteins with their corresponding literature references: PIK3CA:PIK3R1, PIK3CA:PIK3R2, PIK3CA:PIK3R3 (Dey et al. 1998, Vanhaesebroeck et al. 1997, Meier et al. 2004); PIK3CB:PIK3R1, PIK3CB:PIK3R2, PIK3CB:PIK3R3 (Meier et al. 2004); PIK3CD:PIK3R1, PIK3CD:PIK3R2, PIK3CD:PIK3R3 (Vanhaesebroeck et al. 1997, Meier et al. 2004); and PIK3CG:PIK3R5, PIK3CG:PIK3R6 (Voigt et al. 2006, Suire et al. 2005, Stoyanov et al. 1995).\"}]}" ;
