\": \"Presence of PI(3,5)P2 stimulates the maturation of the early endosome into the late endosome\", \"followingEvent\": [1676065], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Presence of PI(3,5)P2 stimulates the maturation of the early endosome into the late endosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676041\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676041.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1675910, \"displayName\": \"PI3P is phosphorylated to PI(3,5)P2 by PIKFYVE at the late endosome membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1676065], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI3P is phosphorylated to PI(3,5)P2 by PIKFYVE at the late endosome membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675910\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675910.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676065\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676065.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1676015, \"displayName\": \"At the late endosome membrane, myotubularin (MTM1), myotubul...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"At the late endosome membrane, myotubularin (MTM1), myotubularin-related protein 2 (MTMR2), myotubularin-related protein 4 (MTMR4), and  myotubularin-related protein 7 (MTMR7) dephosphorylate phosphatidylinositol 3,5-bisphosphate (PI(3,5)P2) to phosphatidylinositol 5-phosphate (PI5P).<br><br>The following lists the above proteins with their corresponding literature references: MTM1 (Cao et al. 2007, Cao et al. 2008, Tsujita et al. 2004, Tronchere et al. 2004), MTMR2 (Cao et al. 2008), MTMR4 (Lorenzo et al. 2006), and MTMR7 (Mochizuki & Majerus 2003, Lorenzo et al. 2006).\"}]}" ;
