he Golgi membrane to the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675815\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675815.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1676177, \"displayName\": \"PI(4,5)P2 is dephosphorylated to PI4P by SYNJ/INPP5[1] at the plasma membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1676109], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI(4,5)P2 is dephosphorylated to PI4P by SYNJ/INPP5[1] at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676177\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676177.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1676149, \"displayName\": \"PI(3,4)P2 is dephosphorylated to PI4P by PTEN at the plasma membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1676109], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI(3,4)P2 is dephosphorylated to PI4P by PTEN at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676149\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676149.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1675780, \"displayName\": \"PI is phosphorylated to PI4P by PI4K2A/B at the plasma membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [1676109], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI is phosphorylated to PI4P by PI4K2A/B at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675780\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675780.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676109\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676109.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 1676171, \"displayName\": \"At the plasma membrane, phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphat...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"At the plasma membrane, phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate (PI(4,5)P2) 3-kinase catalytic subunits form complexes with regulatory subunits.  These complexes along with phosphatidylinositol-4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunits alpha (PIK3C2A), beta (PIK3C2B), and gamma (PIK3C2G) phosphorylate phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate (PI4P) to phosphatidylinositol 3,4-bisphosphate (PI(3,4)P2).  The PI(4,5)P2 3-kinase complexes involved are: PI(4,5)P2 3-kinase catalytic subunit alpha isoform (PIK3CA) bound to PI 3-kinase regulatory subunit alpha/beta/gamma (PIK3R1/2/3); beta (PIK3CB) bound to PIK3R1/2/3; delta (PIK3CD) bound to PIK3R1/2/3; and gamma (PIK3CG) bound to PI 3-kinase regulatory subunit 5 (PIK3R5) or 6 (PIK3R6).<br><br>The following lists the above proteins with their corresponding literature references: PIK3C2A (Arcaro et al. 2000); PIK3C2B (Arcaro et al. 2000, Arcaro et al. 1998); PIK3C2G (Misawa et al. 1998, Ono et al. 1998); PIK3CA:PIK3R1, PIK3CA:PIK3R2, PIK3CA:PIK3R3 (Vanhaesebroeck et al. 1997); PIK3CB:PIK3R1, PIK3CB:PIK3R2, PIK3CB:PIK3R3 (Meier et al. 2004, Guo et al. 1997); PIK3CD:PIK3R1, PIK3CD:PIK3R2, PIK3CD:PIK3R3 (Vanhaesebroeck et al. 1997); and PIK3CG:PIK3R5, PIK3CG:PIK3R6 (Suire et al. 2005, Stoyanov et al. 1995).\"}]}" ;
