-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-191382\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-191382.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 191324, \"displayName\": \"DMAPP [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"DMAPP\", \"prenyl diphosphate(3-)\", \"Dimethylallyl pyrophosphate\", \"prenyl diphosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [191382], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-191324\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-191324.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 191414, \"displayName\": \"MVD decarboxylates MVA5PP to IPPP\", \"followingEvent\": [191382], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"MVD decarboxylates MVA5PP to IPPP\", \"(R)-5-diphosphomevalonate + ATP => isopentenyl diphosphate + ADP + phosphate + CO2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-02-20\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-191414\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-191414.5\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-02-20\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-191382\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-191382.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 191289, \"displayName\": \"Cytosolic  Isopentenyl-diphosphate delta-isomerase isoforms ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Cytosolic  Isopentenyl-diphosphate delta-isomerase isoforms 1 and 2 (IDI1 or 2)) catalyze an essential activation step in the isoprenoid biosynthetic pathway, rearranging isopentenyl pyrophosphate (IPPP) into its highly electrophilic isomer, dimethylallyl pyrophosphate (DMAPP) (Hahn et al. 1996). IPP isomerase may also be located in human peroxisomes but its function there is not clear.\"}]}" ;
