\", \"beta-Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"TPN\", \"Triphosphopyridine nucleotide\"], \"producedByEvent\": [192160], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29366\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29366.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 192033, \"displayName\": \"4-cholesten-7alpha-ol-3-one is reduced to 5beta-cholestan-7alpha-ol-3-one\", \"followingEvent\": [192160], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"4-cholesten-7alpha-ol-3-one is reduced to 5beta-cholestan-7alpha-ol-3-one\", \"7alpha-hydroxycholest-4-en-3-one + H(+) + NADPH => 7alpha-hydroxy-5beta-cholestan-3-one + NADP(+)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-192033\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-192033.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-192160\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-192160.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 192057, \"displayName\": \"5Beta-cholesten-7alpha-ol-3-one and NADPH + H+ form 5beta-ch...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"5Beta-cholesten-7alpha-ol-3-one and NADPH + H+ form 5beta-cholestan-3alpha,7alpha-diol and NAPDP+. The reaction is catalyzed by 3alpha-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase (AKR1C4), a cytosolic enzyme belonging to the aldo-keto reductase family (Dufort et al. 2001). Biochemical studies with rat proteins raise the possibility that other related enzymes may also carry out this reaction in vivo (Russell 2003).\"}]}" ;
