    mslm:evidenceJson "{\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"compartment\": [{\"accession\": \"0005886\", \"className\": \"Compartment\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 876, \"definition\": \"The membrane surrounding a cell that separates the cell from its external environment. It consists of a phospholipid bilayer and associated proteins.\", \"displayName\": \"plasma membrane\", \"name\": \"plasma membrane\", \"schemaClass\": \"Compartment\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0005886\"}], \"dbId\": 193812, \"displayName\": \"Efflux of 27-hydroxycholesterol\", \"followingEvent\": [193801], \"goBiologicalProcess\": {\"accession\": \"0015918\", \"className\": \"GO_BiologicalProcess\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 22603, \"definition\": \"The directed movement of sterols into, out of or within a cell, or between cells, by means of some agent such as a transporter or pore. Sterols are steroids with one or more hydroxyl groups and a hydrocarbon side-chain in the molecule.\", \"displayName\": \"sterol transport\", \"name\": \"sterol transport\", \"schemaClass\": \"GO_BiologicalProcess\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0015918\"}, \"input\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"consumedByEvent\": [193812], \"dbId\": 193846, \"displayName\": \"27OH-CHOL [mitochondrial matrix]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"27OH-CHOL\", \"26-hydroxycholesterol\", \"27-hydroxycholesterol\"], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-193846\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-193846.4\"}], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Efflux of 27-hydroxycholesterol\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 193804, \"displayName\": \"27OH-CHOL [extracellular region]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"27OH-CHOL\", \"26-hydroxycholesterol\", \"27-hydroxycholesterol\"], \"producedByEvent\": [193812], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-193804\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-193804.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 192123, \"displayName\": \"CYP27A1 27-hydroxylates CHOL\", \"followingEvent\": [193812], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP27A1 27-hydroxylates CHOL\", \"cholesterol + H(+) + NADPH + O2 => 26-hydroxycholesterol + H2O + NADP(+)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-192123\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-192123.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-193812\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-193812.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 193837, \"displayName\": \"27-hydroxycholesterol is transported from the mitochondrial ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"27-hydroxycholesterol is transported from the mitochondrial matrix to the extracellular space. In humans, this event is the major source of 27-hydroxycholesterol in the blood and is the means by which the molecule, generated from cholesterol in a variety of cell types, notably macrophages, is transported to the liver for conversion to bile acids and bile salts (Babiker et al. 1999; Bjorkhem et al. 1994). While transport proteins are likely to play a role in this process, the relevant proteins have not been identified.\"}]}" ;
