Cholesten-7alpha,12alpha,27-triol-3-one\", \"4-Cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one + NADPH + H+ + O2 => 4-Cholesten-7alpha,12alpha,27-triol-3-one + NADP+ + H2O\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-193845\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-193845.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10007657, \"displayName\": \"CYP8B1 12-hydroxylates 4CHOL7a,27DONE\", \"inferredFrom\": [193845], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP8B1 12-hydroxylates 4CHOL7a,27DONE\", \"4-Cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one is 12alpha-hydroxylated to 4-Cholesten-7alpha,12alpha,27-triol-3-one\", \"4-Cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one + NADPH + H+ + O2 => 4-Cholesten-7alpha,12alpha,27-triol-3-one + NADP+ + H2O\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-193845\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-193845.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 9617026, \"displayName\": \"4CHOL7a,12a,27TONE [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"4CHOL7a,12a,27TONE\", \"7alpha,12alpha,26-trihydroxycholest-4-en-3-one\"], \"producedByEvent\": [193845], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9617026\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9617026.3\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29366, \"displayName\": \"NADP+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADP+\", \"NADP(3-)\", \"NADP\", \"NADP(+)\", \"Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"beta-Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"TPN\", \"Triphosphopyridine nucleotide\"], \"producedByEvent\": [193845], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29366\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29366.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29356, \"displayName\": \"H2O [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H2O\", \"water\"], \"producedByEvent\": [193845], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29356\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29356.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 193816, \"displayName\": \"Cholest-5-ene-3beta,7alpha,27-triol is oxidized and isomerized to 4-cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one\", \"followingEvent\": [193845], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Cholest-5-ene-3beta,7alpha,27-triol is oxidized and isomerized to 4-cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one\", \"Cholest-5-ene-3beta,7alpha,27-triol + NAD+ => 4-cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one +NADH + H+\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-193816\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-193816.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-193845\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-193845.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 193838, \"displayName\": \"Sterol 12alpha hydroxylase (CYP8B1), associated with the end...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Sterol 12alpha hydroxylase (CYP8B1), associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane, catalyses the 12-alpha-hydroxylation of 4-Cholesten-7alpha,27-diol-3-one (4CHOL7a,27DONE) to 4-Cholesten-7alpha,12alpha,27-triol-3-one. While the human gene has been cloned (Gafvels et al. 1999), its protein product has not been characterised, and the enzymatic properties of human CYP8B1 protein are inferred from those of its well-characterised rabbit homolog (Ishida et al. 1992).\\n\\nThese papers support Reaction:192157 \\\"CYP8B1 12-hydroxylates 4CHOL7aOLONE\\\" but not this one, so this reaction has been set to _doRelease = false.\"}]}" ;
