SLCO1B3 transports ALB:(GCCA, TCCA) from extracellular region to cytosol\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-194079\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-194079.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Set\", \"dbId\": 194097, \"displayName\": \"GCCA, TCCA [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"GCCA, TCCA\", \"cholate bile salts\", \"glycocholate; taurocholate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [194079], \"schemaClass\": \"DefinedSet\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-194097\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-194097.1\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 194153, \"displayName\": \"ABCC3 transports bile salts from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"followingEvent\": [194079], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ABCC3 transports bile salts from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"Efflux of bile salts from enterocytes to portal system by MRP3\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194153\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194153.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194079\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194079.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 194106, \"displayName\": \"A molecule of extracellular glycocholate or taurocholate is ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"A molecule of extracellular glycocholate or taurocholate is transported into the cytosol, mediated by OATP-8 (SLCO1B3) in the plasma membrane. Glycocholate and taurocholate exist in the blood as complexes with serum albumin, and their uptake by OATP-8 must involve disruption of these complexes, but the molecular mechanism coupling disruption and uptake is unknown. In the body, OATP-8 is expressed on the basolateral surfaces of hepatocytes and may play a role in the uptake of glycocholate and taurocholate by the liver under physiological conditions (Kullak-Ublick et al. 2004; Trauner and Boyer 2002).\"}]}" ;
