co-transport bile salts and Na+ from extracellular region to cytosol\", \"NTCP takes up bile salts and Na+ into the liver\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-194121\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-194121.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 83910, \"displayName\": \"Na+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Na+\", \"sodium(1+)\", \"sodium ion\", \"Sodium\"], \"producedByEvent\": [194121, 194121], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-83910\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-83910.4\"}, 83910, {\"className\": \"Set\", \"dbId\": 194156, \"displayName\": \"bile salts and acids [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"bile salts and acids\"], \"producedByEvent\": [194121], \"schemaClass\": \"DefinedSet\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-194156\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-194156.2\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 194153, \"displayName\": \"ABCC3 transports bile salts from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"followingEvent\": [194121], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ABCC3 transports bile salts from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"Efflux of bile salts from enterocytes to portal system by MRP3\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194153\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194153.3\"}, {\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9733545, \"displayName\": \"Bile salts and acids bind ALB\", \"followingEvent\": [194121], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Bile salts and acids bind ALB\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2021-09-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9733545\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9733545.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194121\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194121.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 194091, \"displayName\": \"A molecule of extracellular bile salt (glyco- or taurocholat...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"A molecule of extracellular bile salt (glyco- or taurocholate, or glyco- or taurochenodeoxycholate) and two sodium ions are transported into the cytosol, mediated by NTCP (Na+ / taurocholate cotransporter) in the plasma membrane. Bile salts exist in the blood as complexes with serum albumin, and their uptake by NTCP must involve disruption of this complex, but the molecular mechanism of the coupling of the release of a bile salt from albumin to its uptake by NTCP is unknown. In the body, NTCP is expressed on the basolateral surfaces of hepatocytes, and this reaction is the major route by which bile salts reaborbed from the intestinal lumen into the portal circulation are recovered by the liver (Kullak-Ublick et al. 2004; Trauner and Boyer 2002).\"}]}" ;
