flux) of bile salts and acids by OATP-A\", \"inferredFrom\": [194130], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Transport (influx) of bile salts and acids by OATP-A\", \"SLCO1A2 transports\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-194130\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-194130.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10128749, \"displayName\": \"Transport (influx) of bile salts and acids by OATP-A\", \"inferredFrom\": [194130], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Transport (influx) of bile salts and acids by OATP-A\", \"SLCO1A2 transports\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-194130\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-194130.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10007732, \"displayName\": \"Transport (influx) of bile salts and acids by OATP-A\", \"inferredFrom\": [194130], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Transport (influx) of bile salts and acids by OATP-A\", \"SLCO1A2 transports\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-194130\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-194130.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Set\", \"dbId\": 194156, \"displayName\": \"bile salts and acids [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"bile salts and acids\"], \"producedByEvent\": [194130], \"schemaClass\": \"DefinedSet\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-194156\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-194156.2\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 194153, \"displayName\": \"ABCC3 transports bile salts from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"followingEvent\": [194130], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ABCC3 transports bile salts from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"Efflux of bile salts from enterocytes to portal system by MRP3\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194153\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194153.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194130\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194130.5\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 194087, \"displayName\": \"A molecule of extracellular bile salt (glyco- or taurocholat...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"A molecule of extracellular bile salt (glyco- or taurocholate or taurochenodeoxycholate) or bile acid (cholate or chenodeoxycholate) is transported into the cytosol, mediated by OATP-A (SLCO1A2) in the plasma membrane. Bile salts and acids exist in the blood as complexes with serum albumin, and their uptake by OATP-A must involve disruption of this complex, but the molecular mechanism coupling release of a bile salt or acid from albumin to its uptake by OATP-A is unknown. In the body, OATP-A is expressed only at low levels on the basolateral surfaces of hepatocytes and may play only a minor role in the uptake of bile salts and acids by the liver (Kullak-Ublick et al. 2004; Trauner and Boyer 2002).\"}]}" ;
