hylzymosterol + CO2 + NADPH\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-194642\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-194642.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10007837, \"displayName\": \"4-methyl,4-carboxycholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol is decarboxylated and oxidized to form 4-methylcholesta-8(9),24-dien-3-one\", \"inferredFrom\": [194642], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"4-methyl,4-carboxycholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol is decarboxylated and oxidized to form 4-methylcholesta-8(9),24-dien-3-one\", \"4beta-methylzymosterol-4alpha-carboxylate + NADP(+) => 3-dehydro-4-methylzymosterol + CO2 + NADPH\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-194642\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-194642.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 194667, \"displayName\": \"dh4MZYMOL [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"dh4MZYMOL\", \"3-dehydro-4-methylzymosterol\", \"4-methylcholesta-8(9),24-dien-3-one\"], \"producedByEvent\": [194642], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-194667\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-194667.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 70106, \"displayName\": \"H+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H+\", \"hydron\", \"proton\"], \"producedByEvent\": [194642], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-70106\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-70106.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 113528, \"displayName\": \"CO2 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CO2\", \"carbon dioxide\"], \"producedByEvent\": [194642], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-113528\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-113528.3\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29364, \"displayName\": \"NADPH [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADPH\", \"NADPH(4-)\", \"TPNH\"], \"producedByEvent\": [194642], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29364\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29364.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 194641, \"displayName\": \"4,4-dimethylcholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol is oxidized to 4-methyl,4-carboxycholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol\", \"followingEvent\": [194642], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"4,4-dimethylcholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol is oxidized to 4-methyl,4-carboxycholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol\", \"4,4-dimethylcholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol + 3 NADPH + 3 H+ + 3 O2 => 4-methyl,4-carboxycholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol + 3 NADP+ + 4 H2O\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-02-20\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194641\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194641.4\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2007-02-20\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194642\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194642.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 194655, \"displayName\": \"4-methyl,4-carboxycholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol and NAD+ re...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"4-methyl,4-carboxycholesta-8(9),24-dien-3beta-ol and NAD+ react to form 4-methylcholesta-8(9),24-dien-3-one, CO2, and NADH + H+. This reaction occurs in the endoplasmic reticulum, catalyzed by NSDHL (Caldas and Herman 2003). Defects in this enzyme are associated with CHILD syndrome (Congenital Hemidysplasia with Ichthyosiform nevus and Limb Defects) (Konig et al. 2000), but cholesterol biosynthesis in cells and tissues from affected individuals has not been characterized. Instead, the mechanism and stoichiometry of the reaction are inferred from biochemical studies of partially purified rat enzyme (Rahimtula and Gaylor 1972).\"}]}" ;
