1366, \"displayName\": \"Squalene 2,3-epoxide cyclizes, forming lanosterol\", \"followingEvent\": [194678], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Squalene 2,3-epoxide cyclizes, forming lanosterol\", \"(S)-2,3-epoxysqualene => lanosterol\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-02-20\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-191366\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-191366.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-02-20\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-194678\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-194678.5\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 194660, \"displayName\": \"Lanosterol 14-alpha demethylase (CYP51A1) catalyses oxidativ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Lanosterol 14-alpha demethylase (CYP51A1) catalyses oxidative C14-demethylation of lanosterol (LAN) to  4,4-dimethylcholesta-8(9),14,24-trien-3beta-ol (4,4DMCHOLtrienol). Although the reaction is annotated here as a single concerted event, studies with purified rat enzyme indicate that the methyl group is converted successively to an alcohol and an aldehyde before being released as formate (Stromstedt et al. 1996, Strushkevich et al. 2010).\"}]}" ;
