rmembrane space\", \"cholesterol(in) = cholesterol(out)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Xenopus tropicalis\", \"stId\": \"R-XTR-196126\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-XTR-196126.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10581116, \"displayName\": \"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"inferredFrom\": [196126], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"cholesterol(in) = cholesterol(out)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-196126\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-196126.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10471271, \"displayName\": \"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"inferredFrom\": [196126], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"cholesterol(in) = cholesterol(out)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-196126\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-196126.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10356467, \"displayName\": \"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"inferredFrom\": [196126], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"cholesterol(in) = cholesterol(out)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-196126\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-196126.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10249281, \"displayName\": \"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"inferredFrom\": [196126], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"cholesterol(in) = cholesterol(out)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-196126\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-196126.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10129086, \"displayName\": \"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"inferredFrom\": [196126], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"cholesterol(in) = cholesterol(out)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-196126\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-196126.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10008026, \"displayName\": \"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"inferredFrom\": [196126], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STAR mediates CHOL translocation from cytosol to mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"cholesterol(in) = cholesterol(out)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-196126\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-196126.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Set\", \"dbId\": 196094, \"displayName\": \"STARD3:STARD3NL, STARD4,6 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 3, \"name\": [\"STARD3:STARD3NL, STARD4,6\", \"StAR-related cholesterol-binding proteins\"], \"producedByEvent\": [196126], \"schemaClass\": \"CandidateSet\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-196094\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-196094.2\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 193156, \"displayName\": \"CHOL [mitochondrial inner membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CHOL\", \"cholesterol\"], \"producedByEvent\": [196126], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-193156\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-193156.5\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-196126\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-196126.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 193130, \"displayName\": \"CHOL (cholesterol) traverses the cytosol and the mitochondri...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"CHOL (cholesterol) traverses the cytosol and the mitochondrial intermembrane space complexed with STARD cholesterol-binding proteins. A plausible model, supported by studies in vitro and in cells overexpressing cloned human proteins, is that cytosolic STARD proteins bind cholesterol liberated from lysosomes or cytosolic lipid droplets and carry it to the outer mitochondrial membrane (Rodriguez-Aguado et al. 2005; Soccio et al. 2002), where STAR steroidogenic acute regulatory protein mediates its delivery to the mitochondrial inner membrane (Miller 2007, Letourneau et al. 2015).<p>This process is essential for steroid hormone synthesis. Mutations in the gene encoding STAR block synthesis of all steroid hormones in humans (Bose et al. 1996). The transport step is also a key site for normal regulation of steroid hormone synthesis, as STAR protein is unstable and its synthesis is up-regulated in response to signals such as the binding of ACTH to its receptors on adrenal cells (Stocco 2001).\"}]}" ;
