-ol is desaturated to form cholesta-5,7,24-trien-3beta-ol\", \"followingEvent\": [196402], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Cholesta-7,24-dien-3beta-ol is desaturated to form cholesta-5,7,24-trien-3beta-ol\", \"5alpha-cholesta-7,24-dien-3beta-ol + NADPH + O2 + H(+) => 7-dehydrodesmosterol + NADP(+) + 2 H2O\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-02-20\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-195664\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-195664.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-02-20\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-196402\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-196402.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 196416, \"displayName\": \"Cholesta-5,7,24-trien-3beta-ol and NADPH + H+ react to form ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Cholesta-5,7,24-trien-3beta-ol and NADPH + H+ react to form desmosterol and NADP+. This reaction is catalyzed by DHCR7, associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane. The biochemical details of the reaction are inferred from those of the reaction catalyzed by the well-studied rat enzyme (Bae et al. 1999).\"}]}" ;
