H\", \"coenzyme A(4-)\", \"coenzyme A\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2046088], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-162743\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-162743.6\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2046084, \"displayName\": \"Desaturation of alpha-linoleoyl-CoA to Stearidonoyl-CoA\", \"followingEvent\": [2046088], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Desaturation of alpha-linoleoyl-CoA to Stearidonoyl-CoA\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2046084\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2046084.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2046088\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2046088.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2045956, \"displayName\": \"SDA-CoA (6,9,12,15-18:4(n-3)) is rapidly elongated by two ca...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"SDA-CoA (6,9,12,15-18:4(n-3)) is rapidly elongated by two carbon atoms to 8,11,14,17-eicosatetraenoyl-CoA (8,11,14,17-20:4(n-3), ETA-CoA). The  NADPH-consuming enzyme long-chain fatty acyl elongase (ELOVL5) mediates this reaction which and adds malonyl-CoA to the SDA-CoA and releases carbon dioxide and free CoA (Leonard et al. 2004). \"}]}" ;
