": \"R-MMU-2046100.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 2046057, \"displayName\": \"DPA-CoA [endoplasmic reticulum lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"DPA-CoA\", \"(7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-docosapentaenoyl-CoA\", \"7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z-docosapentaenoyl-CoA (DPA-CoA)\", \"docosapentaenoyl-CoA\", \"7,10,13,16,19-22:5(n-3)\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2046100], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-2046057\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-2046057.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 159751, \"displayName\": \"CO2 [endoplasmic reticulum lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CO2\", \"carbon dioxide\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2046100], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-159751\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-159751.3\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 162743, \"displayName\": \"CoA-SH [endoplasmic reticulum lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CoA-SH\", \"coenzyme A(4-)\", \"coenzyme A\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2046100], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-162743\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-162743.6\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 113519, \"displayName\": \"H2O [endoplasmic reticulum lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H2O\", \"water\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2046100], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-113519\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-113519.3\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 113564, \"displayName\": \"NADP+ [endoplasmic reticulum lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADP+\", \"NADP(+)\", \"NADP\", \"Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"beta-Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"TPN\", \"Triphosphopyridine nucleotide\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2046100, 2046100], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-113564\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-113564.4\"}, 113564], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2046089, \"displayName\": \"Desaturation of eicosatetraenoyl-CoA to eicosapentaenoyl-CoA\", \"followingEvent\": [2046100], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Desaturation of eicosatetraenoyl-CoA to eicosapentaenoyl-CoA\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2046089\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2046089.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2046100\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2046100.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2045957, \"displayName\": \"Eicosapentaenoyl-CoA (EPA-CoA) is transformed to docosapenta...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Eicosapentaenoyl-CoA (EPA-CoA) is transformed to docosapentaenoyl-CoA (DPA-CoA/clupanodonic acid; 7,10,13,16,19-22:5(n-3)) by addition of two carbon atoms from malanoyl-CoA. This reaction is catalyzed by the enzymes ELOVL5/2 (Leonard et al. 2004). DPA is quite high in seal oil and may act as an anti-atherogenic factor. DPA has 10-fold greater endothelial cell migration ability than EPA, which is important in wound-healing processes. DPA may act as a precursor for production of the DPA-related  D-series of resolvins or neuroprotectins (Kaur et al. 2011).\"}]}" ;
