s VD3 to 25(OH)D\", \"inferredFrom\": [209845], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP2R1 25-hydroxylates VD3 to 25(OH)D\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-209845\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-209845.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 8963879, \"displayName\": \"25(OH)D [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"25(OH)D\", \"calcidiol\", \"CDL\", \"25-hydroxyvitamin D3\"], \"producedByEvent\": [209845], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-8963879\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-8963879.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29356, \"displayName\": \"H2O [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H2O\", \"water\"], \"producedByEvent\": [209845], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29356\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29356.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29366, \"displayName\": \"NADP+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADP+\", \"NADP(3-)\", \"NADP\", \"NADP(+)\", \"Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"beta-Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"TPN\", \"Triphosphopyridine nucleotide\"], \"producedByEvent\": [209845], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29366\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29366.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 350147, \"displayName\": \"VD3 translocates from extracellular region to ER membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [209845], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VD3 translocates from extracellular region to ER membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-06-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-350147\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-350147.5\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-06-30\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-209845\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-209845.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 215578, \"displayName\": \"To be functionally active, vitamin D3 (VD3) needs to be dihy...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"To be functionally active, vitamin D3 (VD3) needs to be dihydroxylated. The first hydroxylation at position 25 is carried out by ER membrane-located vitamin D 25-hydroxylase (CYP2R1) in the liver, forming 25-hydroxyvitamin D (calcidiol, 25(OH)D) (Shinkyo et al. 2004, Cheng et al. 2003).\"}]}" ;
