GH2 is isomerised to PGD2 by PTGDS\", \"prostaglandin H2 => prostaglandin D2”\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-2161620\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-2161620.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10283453, \"displayName\": \"PGH2 is isomerised to PGD2 by PTGDS\", \"inferredFrom\": [2161620], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGH2 is isomerised to PGD2 by PTGDS\", \"prostaglandin H2 => prostaglandin D2”\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-2161620\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-2161620.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10170354, \"displayName\": \"PGH2 is isomerised to PGD2 by PTGDS\", \"inferredFrom\": [2161620], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGH2 is isomerised to PGD2 by PTGDS\", \"prostaglandin H2 => prostaglandin D2”\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-2161620\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-2161620.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10048460, \"displayName\": \"PGH2 is isomerised to PGD2 by PTGDS\", \"inferredFrom\": [2161620], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGH2 is isomerised to PGD2 by PTGDS\", \"prostaglandin H2 => prostaglandin D2”\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-2161620\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-2161620.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 2161634, \"displayName\": \"PGD2 [endoplasmic reticulum lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGD2\", \"prostaglandin D2(1-)\", \"prostaglandin D2\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2161620], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-2161634\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-2161634.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 140359, \"displayName\": \"PGG2 is reduced to PGH2 by PTGS1\", \"followingEvent\": [2161620], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGG2 is reduced to PGH2 by PTGS1\", \"AH2 + prostaglandin G2 = A + H2O + prostaglandin H2\", \"Peroxidative reduction of PGG2 to PGH2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-06-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-140359\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-140359.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2309773, \"displayName\": \"PGG2 is reduced to PGH2 by PTGS2\", \"followingEvent\": [2161620], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGG2 is reduced to PGH2 by PTGS2\", \"AH2 + prostaglandin G2 = A + H2O + prostaglandin H2\", \"Peroxidative reduction of PGG2 to PGH2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-06-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2309773\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2309773.8\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-12-04\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2161620\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2161620.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2161622, \"displayName\": \"Prostaglandin D2 (PGD2) is a structural isomer of prostaglan...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Prostaglandin D2 (PGD2) is a structural isomer of prostaglandin E2 (PGE2).  There is a 9-keto and 11-hydroxy group on PGE2 with these substituents reversed on PGD2.  PGD2 is formed by two evolutionarily distinct, but functionally convergent, prostaglandin D synthases: lipocalin-type prostaglandin-D synthase aka Prostaglandin-H2 D-isomerase (PTDGS) and hematopoietic prostaglandin D synthase (HPGDS).  One of the main differences between these two proteins is that HPGDS requires glutathione (GSH) for catalysis while PTDGS can function without this cofactor.  Here, PTDGS promotes the isomerisation of prostaglandin H2 (PGH2) to prostaglandin D2 (PGD2) (Zhou et al. 2010).\"}]}" ;
