": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-265287\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-265287.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"uncertain\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2299725, \"displayName\": \"PGH2 diffuses from the endoplasmic reticulum lumen to the cytosol\", \"followingEvent\": [2161660], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGH2 diffuses from the endoplasmic reticulum lumen to the cytosol\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-12-04\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2299725\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2299725.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-12-04\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2161660\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2161660.5\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2161728, \"displayName\": \"Prostaglandin E synthase (PTGES) requires glutathione (GSH) ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Prostaglandin E synthase (PTGES) requires glutathione (GSH) as an essential cofactor for its enzymatic activity, and together they isomerise prostaglandin H2 (PGH2) to prostaglandin E2 (PGE2) (Jegerschold et al. 2008).  After PGH2 has been produced by the prostaglandin G/H synthases (PTGS1 and 2) on the lumenal side of the endoplasmic reticulum, it diffuses through the membrane to the active site of PTGES located on the cytoplasmic side.\"}]}" ;
