icosanoids by a specific dehydrogenase in human polymorphonuclear leukocytes\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"19233-41\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 1326548, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Metabolism of 5(S)-hydroxy-6,8,11,14-eicosatetraenoic acid and other 5(S)-hydroxyeicosanoids by a specific dehydrogenase in human polymorphonuclear leukocytes\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1326548\", \"volume\": 267, \"year\": 1992}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"5S-HETE is oxidised to 5-oxoETE by 5-HEDH\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 2161921, \"displayName\": \"5-oxoETE [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"5-oxoETE\", \"5-oxo-ETE(1-)\", \"5-oxo-ETE\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2161776], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-2161921\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-2161921.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29364, \"displayName\": \"NADPH [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADPH\", \"NADPH(4-)\", \"TPNH\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2161776], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29364\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29364.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 70106, \"displayName\": \"H+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H+\", \"hydron\", \"proton\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2161776], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-70106\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-70106.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2161946, \"displayName\": \"5S-HpETE is reduced to 5S-HETE by GPX1/2/4\", \"followingEvent\": [2161776], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"5S-HpETE is reduced to 5S-HETE by GPX1/2/4\", \"(5S)-hydroperoxy-(6E,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoate + 2 glutathione => (5S)-hydroxy-(6E,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoate + glutathione disulfide + H2O\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-12-04\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2161946\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2161946.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-03-13\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2161776\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2161776.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2161831, \"displayName\": \"Current literature suggests that 5S-hydroxy-eicosatetraenoic...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Current literature suggests that 5S-hydroxy-eicosatetraenoic acid (5S-HETE) itself does not appear to play a significant role in biological signalling. However, it can be further oxidised by a 5-hydroxy-eicosatetraenoic acid dehydrogenase (5-HEDH) to form the bioactive 5-oxo-eicosatetraenoic acid (5-oxoETE, also known as 5-KETE. While the gene has not yet been cloned, the biophysical properties of the human enzyme have been well characterised (Powell et al. 1992).\"}]}" ;
