one peroxidases (GPXs) in human platelets (either GP...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Glutathione peroxidases (GPXs) in human platelets (either GPX1, GPX2, or GPX4 are present in the cytosol) are involved in reducing 15S-hydroperoxyeicosatetraenoic acid (15S-HpETE) to 15S-hydroxyeicosatetraenoic acid (15S-HETE) (Hill et al. 1989).\"}]}" ;
