lammatory arachidonic acid metabolites produced via the 15-lipoxygenase-1 pathway in human eosinophils and mast cells\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18184802\", \"volume\": 105, \"year\": 2008}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 2161760, \"displayName\": \"Hodgkin Reed-Sternberg cells express 15-lipoxygenase-1 and are putative producers of eoxins in vivo: novel insight into the inflammatory features of classical Hodgkin lymphoma\", \"journal\": \"FEBS J\", \"pages\": \"4222-34\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 18647347, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Hodgkin Reed-Sternberg cells express 15-lipoxygenase-1 and are putative producers of eoxins in vivo: novel insight into the inflammatory features of classical Hodgkin lymphoma\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18647347\", \"volume\": 275, \"year\": 2008}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"EXD4 is converted to EXE4 by DPEP\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 2142730, \"displayName\": \"EXE4 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"EXE4\", \"eoxin E4(1-)\", \"eoxin E4\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2161868], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-2142730\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-2142730.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29424, \"displayName\": \"Gly [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Gly\", \"glycine zwitterion\", \"L-glycine\", \"glycine\", \"Aminoacetic acid\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2161868], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29424\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29424.6\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2161945, \"displayName\": \"EXC4 is converted to EXD4 by GGT\", \"followingEvent\": [2161868], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"EXC4 is converted to EXD4 by GGT\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-12-04\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2161945\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2161945.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-12-04\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2161868\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2161868.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2162033, \"displayName\": \"In an analogous reaction to the formation of leukotriene E4 ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"In an analogous reaction to the formation of leukotriene E4 (LTE4), eoxin D4 (EXD4) is converted to eoxin E4 (EXE4) by a dipeptidase (DPEP) (Feltenmark et al. 2008, Claesson et al. 2008) which has not yet been identified.\"}]}" ;
