ing of lysosomal enzymes\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2960521\", \"volume\": 6, \"year\": 1987}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9841185, \"displayName\": \"In vitro mutagenesis of potential N-glycosylation sites of arylsulfatase A. Effects on glycosylation, phosphorylation, and intracellular sorting\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"13262-6\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 1352293, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"In vitro mutagenesis of potential N-glycosylation sites of arylsulfatase A. Effects on glycosylation, phosphorylation, and intracellular sorting\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1352293\", \"volume\": 267, \"year\": 1992}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 11072017, \"displayName\": \"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\", \"inferredFrom\": [2248891], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Schizosaccharomyces pombe\", \"stId\": \"R-SPO-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SPO-2248891.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10788519, \"displayName\": \"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\", \"inferredFrom\": [2248891], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Gallus gallus\", \"stId\": \"R-GGA-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-GGA-2248891.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10697191, \"displayName\": \"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\", \"inferredFrom\": [2248891], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Xenopus tropicalis\", \"stId\": \"R-XTR-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-XTR-2248891.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10509818, \"displayName\": \"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\", \"inferredFrom\": [2248891], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-2248891.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10394820, \"displayName\": \"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\", \"inferredFrom\": [2248891], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-2248891.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10284774, \"displayName\": \"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\", \"inferredFrom\": [2248891], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-2248891.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10171741, \"displayName\": \"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\", \"inferredFrom\": [2248891], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-2248891.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10049849, \"displayName\": \"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\", \"inferredFrom\": [2248891], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"M6PR transports activated ARSA to the lysosome\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-2248891.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 1606814, \"displayName\": \"active ARSA:Ca2+ [lysosomal lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"active ARSA:Ca2+\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2248891], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1606814\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1606814.1\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1614362, \"displayName\": \"SUMF1 mediates the oxidation of cysteine to formylglycine, producing active arylsulfatases\", \"followingEvent\": [2248891], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SUMF1 mediates the oxidation of cysteine to formylglycine, producing active arylsulfatases\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1614362\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1614362.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2248891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2248891.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2248892, \"displayName\": \"Activated arylsulfatase A (ARSA) is one of many lysosomal en...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Activated arylsulfatase A (ARSA) is one of many lysosomal enzymes bearing phosphomannosyl (M6P) residues. Cation-dependent mannose-6-phosphate receptor (M6PR) binds to M6P on ARSA. The resulting receptor-ligand complex is transported to an acidic pre-lysosomal compartment where the low pH mediates the dissociation of the complex (Stein et al., 1987; Gieselmann et al., 1992).\"}]}" ;
