 reticulum membrane]'\", \"regulatedEntity\": [2309773], \"schemaClass\": \"NegativeRegulation\"}], \"regulationReference\": [{\"className\": \"RegulationReference\", \"dbId\": 9735229, \"displayName\": \"Negative regulation by 'PTGS2 dimer:PTGS2 inhibitors [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]' Flexibility of the NSAID binding site in the structure of human cyclooxygenase-2\", \"schemaClass\": \"RegulationReference\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-06-30\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2309773\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2309773.8\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2309784, \"displayName\": \"Prostaglandin G/H synthase 2 (PTGS2) exhibits a dual catalyt...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Prostaglandin G/H synthase 2 (PTGS2) exhibits a dual catalytic activity, a cyclooxygenase and a peroxidase. The peroxidase function converts prostaglandin G2 (PGG2) to prostaglandin H2 (PGH2) via a two-electron reduction (Hamberg et al. 1973, Hla & Neilson 1992, Swinney et al. 1997, Barnett et al. 1994).\"}]}" ;
