": \"Microarray analyses of SREBP-1a and SREBP-1c target genes identify new regulatory pathways in muscle\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18559965\", \"volume\": 34, \"year\": 2008}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1655609, \"displayName\": \"Differential stimulation of cholesterol and unsaturated fatty acid biosynthesis in cells expressing individual nuclear sterol regulatory element-binding proteins\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"26138-48\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 9748295, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Differential stimulation of cholesterol and unsaturated fatty acid biosynthesis in cells expressing individual nuclear sterol regulatory element-binding proteins\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9748295\", \"volume\": 273, \"year\": 1998}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SREBP1A,2 binds the HMGCR promoter\", \"SREBF1A,2 binds the HMGCR promoter\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 2426128, \"displayName\": \"SREBP1A,2:NF-Y:HMGCR gene [nucleoplasm]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 4, \"name\": [\"SREBP1A,2:NF-Y:HMGCR gene\", \"SREBF1A,2:NF-Y:HMGCR gene\"], \"producedByEvent\": [2426162], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2426128\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2426128.1\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2065539, \"displayName\": \"SREBP1A,1C,2:Importin beta-1 dissociates\", \"followingEvent\": [2426162], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SREBP1A,1C,2:Importin beta-1 dissociates\", \"SREBF1A,1C,2:Importin beta-1 dissociates\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-09-18\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2065539\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2065539.3\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2012-09-18\", \"releaseStatus\": \"UPDATED\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2426162\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2426162.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 2426213, \"displayName\": \"SREBP1A (SREBF1A) or SREBP2, together with NF-Y, bind and tr...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"SREBP1A (SREBF1A) or SREBP2, together with NF-Y, bind and transactivate the promoter of the HMGCR gene (Vallett et al. 1996, Pai et al. 1998, Reed et al. 2008, Rome et al. 2008). SREBP2 activates HMGCR slightly more than does SREBP1A (Pai et al. 1998). SREBP1A/2 binds 2 main sites and 2 auxiliary sites in the HMGCR promoter (Vallett et al. 1996).\"}]}" ;
