GH2 to PGE2\", \"inferredFrom\": [265295], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Prostaglandin E synthase isomerizes PGH2 to PGE2\", \"prostaglandin H2 => prostaglandin E2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-265295\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-265295.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10013374, \"displayName\": \"Prostaglandin E synthase isomerizes PGH2 to PGE2\", \"inferredFrom\": [265295], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Prostaglandin E synthase isomerizes PGH2 to PGE2\", \"prostaglandin H2 => prostaglandin E2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-265295\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-265295.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 265287, \"displayName\": \"PGE2 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGE2\", \"prostaglandin E2(1-)\", \"prostaglandin E2\"], \"producedByEvent\": [265295], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-265287\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-265287.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"uncertain\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2299725, \"displayName\": \"PGH2 diffuses from the endoplasmic reticulum lumen to the cytosol\", \"followingEvent\": [265295], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PGH2 diffuses from the endoplasmic reticulum lumen to the cytosol\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-12-04\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2299725\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2299725.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-12-17\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-265295\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-265295.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 265272, \"displayName\": \"Prostaglandin E2 (PGE2) is the most abundant prostanoid in t...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Prostaglandin E2 (PGE2) is the most abundant prostanoid in the body and is a major mediator of inflammation in diseases such as osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis. The product of arachidonate, prostaglandin H2 (PGH2) serves as the substrate for the isomerization to PGE2. The conversion is carried out by prostaglandin E synthases. Of the three forms, two are predominanly cytosolic. Prostaglandin E synthase 3 (PTGES3) is also called cytosolic prostaglandin E2 synthase (cPGES). Prostaglandin E synthase 2 (mPGES-2, PTGES2) is synthesized as a Golgi membrane-associated protein which undergoes a spontaneous cleavage of the N-terminal hydrophobic domain leading to a truncated mature cytosolic protein.\"}]}" ;
