266046], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"LTC4 is exported from the cytosol by ABCC1\", \"ATP + H2O + leukotriene C4(in) => ADP + H(+) + leukotriene C4(out) + phosphate\", \"ABCC1 mediates LTC4 export from the cell\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-12-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-266070\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-266070.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-12-17\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-266046\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-266046.6\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 266069, \"displayName\": \"The reversible conversion of leukotriene C4 (LTC4) to leukot...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"The reversible conversion of leukotriene C4 (LTC4) to leukotriene D4 (LTD4) is catalysed by gamma-glutamyl transferases 1 (GGT1) and 5 (GGT5). GGTs are present on the outer surface of plasma membranes and are a heterodimer of a heavy and a light chain. Its action involves the hydrolysis of the gamma-glutamyl peptide bond of glutathione and glutathione conjugates, releasing glutamate. In this example, LTC4 is a glutathione conjugate that is hydrolysed to LTD4 (Anderson et al. 1982, Wickham et al. 2011).\"}]}" ;
