    mslm:evidenceJson "{\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"compartment\": [{\"accession\": \"0005789\", \"className\": \"Compartment\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 12045, \"definition\": \"The lipid bilayer surrounding the endoplasmic reticulum.\", \"displayName\": \"endoplasmic reticulum membrane\", \"name\": \"endoplasmic reticulum membrane\", \"schemaClass\": \"Compartment\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0005789\"}, {\"accession\": \"0005576\", \"className\": \"Compartment\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 984, \"definition\": \"The space external to the outermost structure of a cell. For cells without external protective or external encapsulating structures this refers to space outside of the plasma membrane. This term covers the host cell environment outside an intracellular parasite.\", \"displayName\": \"extracellular region\", \"name\": \"extracellular region\", \"schemaClass\": \"Compartment\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0005576\"}], \"dbId\": 350147, \"displayName\": \"VD3 translocates from extracellular region to ER membrane\", \"goBiologicalProcess\": {\"accession\": \"0140354\", \"className\": \"GO_BiologicalProcess\", \"databaseName\": \"GO\", \"dbId\": 9658138, \"definition\": \"The directed movement of a lipid from outside of a cell into a cell. This may occur via transport across the plasma membrane or via endocytosis.\", \"displayName\": \"lipid import into cell\", \"name\": \"lipid import into cell\", \"schemaClass\": \"GO_BiologicalProcess\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0140354\"}, \"input\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"consumedByEvent\": [350147], \"dbId\": 209767, \"displayName\": \"VD3 [extracellular region]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VD3\", \"calciol\", \"Vitamin D3\", \"Cholecalciferol\"], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-209767\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-209767.4\"}], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"literatureReference\": [{\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 209913, \"displayName\": \"Metabolism of vitamin D by human microsomal CYP2R1\", \"journal\": \"Biochem Biophys Res Commun\", \"pages\": \"451-7\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 15465040, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Metabolism of vitamin D by human microsomal CYP2R1\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/15465040\", \"volume\": 324, \"year\": 2004}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VD3 translocates from extracellular region to ER membrane\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 8963870, \"displayName\": \"VD3 [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VD3\", \"calciol\", \"Vitamin D3\", \"Cholecalciferol\"], \"producedByEvent\": [350147], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-8963870\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-8963870.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 8963851, \"displayName\": \"VD3 dissociates from GC\", \"followingEvent\": [350147], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VD3 dissociates from GC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2017-09-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8963851\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8963851.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-06-30\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-350147\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-350147.5\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 350134, \"displayName\": \"Once vitamin D3 (VD3) is released from vitamin D binding pro...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Once vitamin D3 (VD3) is released from vitamin D binding protein (GC, DBP), it translocates from the extracellular region to the ER membrane, becoming available for hydroxylation by the microsomal enzyme CYP2R1 (Shinkyo et al. 2004).\"}]}" ;
