ylcholine catabolic process\", \"name\": \"acetylcholine catabolic process\", \"schemaClass\": \"GO_BiologicalProcess\", \"url\": \"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/QuickGO/term/GO:0006581\"}, \"input\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"consumedByEvent\": [372519], \"dbId\": 372533, \"displayName\": \"AcCho [extracellular region]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"AcCho\", \"acetylcholine\", \"O-acetylcholine\"], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-372533\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-372533.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"consumedByEvent\": [372519], \"dbId\": 109276, \"displayName\": \"H2O [extracellular region]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H2O\", \"water\"], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-109276\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-109276.4\"}], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"literatureReference\": [{\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 372541, \"displayName\": \"Rational design of a drug for Alzheimer's disease with cholinesterase inhibitory and neuroprotective activity\", \"journal\": \"Chem Biol Interact\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 18457821, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Rational design of a drug for Alzheimer's disease with cholinesterase inhibitory and neuroprotective activity\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18457821\", \"year\": 2008}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1482734, \"displayName\": \"The effect of elimination of intersubunit disulfide bonds on the activity, assembly, and secretion of recombinant human acetylcholinesterase. Expression of acetylcholinesterase Cys-580----Ala mutant\", \"journal\": \"J Biol Chem\", \"pages\": \"23977-84\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 1748670, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"The effect of elimination of intersubunit disulfide bonds on the activity, assembly, and secretion of recombinant human acetylcholinesterase. Expression of acetylcholinesterase Cys-580----Ala mutant\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1748670\", \"volume\": 266, \"year\": 1991}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 1482716, \"displayName\": \"Structures of recombinant native and E202Q mutant human acetylcholinesterase complexed with the snake-venom toxin fasciculin-II\", \"journal\": \"Acta Crystallogr D Biol Crystallogr\", \"pages\": \"1385-94\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 11053835, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Structures of recombinant native and E202Q mutant human acetylcholinesterase complexed with the snake-venom toxin fasciculin-II\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11053835\", \"volume\": 56, \"year\": 2000}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"AcCho is hydrolyzed to Cho and acetate by ACHE\", \"Acetylcholine clearance from synaptic cleft\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 11016535, \"displayName\": \"AcCho is hydrolyzed to Cho and acetate by ACHE\", \"inferredFrom\": [372519], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"AcCho is hydrolyzed to Cho and acetate by ACHE\", \"Acetylcholine clearance from synaptic cleft\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Dictyostelium discoideum\", \"stId\": \"R-DDI-372519\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DDI-372519.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10939694, \"displayName\": \"AcCho is hydrolyzed to Cho and acetate by ACHE\", \"inferredFrom\": [372519], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"AcCho is hydrolyzed to Cho and acetate by ACHE\", \"Acetylcholine clearance from synaptic cleft\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-372519\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-372519.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10854935, \"displayName\": \"AcCho is hydrolyzed to Cho and acetate by ACHE\", \"inferredFrom\": [372519], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"AcCho is hydrolyzed to Cho and acetate by ACHE\", \"Acetylcholine clearance from synaptic cleft\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Drosophila melanogaster\", \"stId\": \"R-DME-372519\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DME-372519.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 264638, \"displayName\": \"Cho [extracellular region]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Cho\", \"choline\"], \"producedByEvent\": [372519], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-264638\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-264638.3\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1524044, \"displayName\": \"acetate [extracellular region]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"acetate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [372519], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1524044\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1524044.2\"}], \"regulatedBy\": [{\"className\": \"NegativeRegulation\", \"dbId\": 9634836, \"displayName\": \"Negative regulation by 'ACHE:ACHEIs [plasma membrane]'\", \"regulatedEntity\": [372519], \"schemaClass\": \"NegativeRegulation\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2008-09-30\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-372519\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-372519.6\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 373212, \"displayName\": \"Acetylcholinesterase (ACHE) oligomers (comprising monomers, ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Acetylcholinesterase (ACHE) oligomers (comprising monomers, dimers and tetramers), anchored to the extracellular side of the plasma membrane, hydrolyze acetylcholine (AcCho) to form choline (Cho) and acetate (Weinstock & Groner 2008, Velan et al. 1991, Kryger et al. 2000).<br><br>Acetylcholine from the synaptic cleft is degraded into inactive molecules, Cho and acetate by ACHE, which is located in the synaptic cleft (Weinstock & Groner 2008).\"}]}" ;
