> 2-hydroxyphytanoyl-CoA + succinate + CO2\", \"followingEvent\": [389611], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"phytanoyl-CoA + 2-oxoglutarate + O2 => 2-hydroxyphytanoyl-CoA + succinate + CO2\", \"2-oxoglutarate + O2 + phytanoyl-CoA => 2-hydroxyphytanoyl-CoA + CO2 + succinate\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-04-01\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-389639\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-389639.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-04-01\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-389611\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-389611.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 389587, \"displayName\": \"Peroxisomal HACL1 catalyzes the reaction of 2-hydroxyphytano...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Peroxisomal HACL1 catalyzes the reaction of 2-hydroxyphytanoyl-CoA to form pristanal and formyl-CoA. The active form of the enzyme is a homotetramer, with one Mg++ and one molecule of thiamin pyrophosphate bound to each monomer (Croes et al. 1997; Foulon et al. 1999).\"}]}" ;
