-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA + H2O => 3-hydroxypristanoyl-CoA\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-389986\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-389986.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 389982, \"displayName\": \"3-hydroxypristanoyl-CoA [peroxisomal matrix]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"3-hydroxypristanoyl-CoA\"], \"producedByEvent\": [389986], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-389982\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-389982.2\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 389889, \"displayName\": \"ACOX2:FAD, ACOXL:FAD oxidise (2S)-pristanoyl-CoA to trans-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA\", \"followingEvent\": [389986], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ACOX2:FAD, ACOXL:FAD oxidise (2S)-pristanoyl-CoA to trans-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA\", \"(2S)-pristanoyl-CoA + O2 => (2E)-pristenoyl-CoA + H2O2\", \"(2S)-pristanoyl-CoA + O2 => trans-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA + H2O2 (ACOX2)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-04-01\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-389889\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-389889.4\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 389891, \"displayName\": \"(2S)-pristanoyl-CoA + O2 => trans-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA + H2O2 (ACOX3)\", \"followingEvent\": [389986], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"(2S)-pristanoyl-CoA + O2 => trans-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA + H2O2 (ACOX3)\", \"(2S)-pristanoyl-CoA + O2 => (2E)-pristenoyl-CoA + H2O2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-04-01\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-389891\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-389891.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-04-01\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-389986\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-389986.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 389998, \"displayName\": \"Peroxisomal HSD17B4 dimer catalyzes the reaction of trans-2,...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Peroxisomal HSD17B4 dimer catalyzes the reaction of trans-2,3-dehydropristanoyl-CoA and H2O to form 3-hydroxypristanoyl-CoA. The enzyme is bifunctional - an aminoterminal domain catalyzes the dehydrogenation of a variety of 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA's and a carboxyterminal domain catalyzes the hydration of a variety of trans-2,3-dehydroacyl-CoA's, the reaction annotated here (Ferdinandusse et al. 2004; Jiang et al. 1996, 1997). Defects in the enzyme are associated with a severe disorder of peroxisomal fatty acid metabolism in humans (Ferdinandusse et al. 2006).\"}]}" ;
