\"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 390256, \"displayName\": \"ACOX1 oxidizes C26:0 CoA\", \"followingEvent\": [390252], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ACOX1 oxidizes C26:0 CoA\", \"hexacosanoyl-CoA + O2 => (2E)-hexacosenoyl-CoA + H2O2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-04-01\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-390256\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-390256.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-04-01\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-390252\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-390252.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 390258, \"displayName\": \"Peroxisomal HSD17B4 dimer catalyzes the reaction of trans-2,...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Peroxisomal HSD17B4 dimer catalyzes the reaction of trans-2,3-dehydrohexacosanoyl-CoA and H2O to form 3-hydroxyhexacosanoyl-CoA. The enzyme is bifunctional - an aminoterminal domain catalyzes the dehydrogenation of a variety of 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA's and a carboxyterminal domain catalyzes the hydration of a variety of trans-2,3-dehydroacyl-CoA's, the reaction annotated here (Jiang et al. 1996, 1997). Defects in the enzyme are associated with a severe disorder of peroxisomal fatty acid metabolism in humans (Ferdinandusse et al. 2006).\"}]}" ;
