ha\"], \"producedByEvent\": [400143], \"schemaClass\": \"DefinedSet\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-400207\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-400207.1\"}, {\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 400154, \"displayName\": \"PPARA:RXRA Coactivator complex [nucleoplasm]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 5, \"name\": [\"PPARA:RXRA Coactivator complex\"], \"producedByEvent\": [400143], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-400154\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-400154.1\"}, {\"className\": \"Protein\", \"dbId\": 1989743, \"displayName\": \"FABP1 [nucleoplasm]\", \"endCoordinate\": 127, \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"FABP1\", \"Fatty acid-binding protein, liver\", \"FABPL_HUMAN\"], \"producedByEvent\": [400143], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceGeneProduct\", \"schemaClass\": \"EntityWithAccessionedSequence\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1989743\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1989743.1\", \"startCoordinate\": 1}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 400183, \"displayName\": \"PPARA:RXRA binds Corepressors of PPARA\", \"followingEvent\": [400143], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PPARA:RXRA binds Corepressors of PPARA\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-400183\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-400183.4\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2026996, \"displayName\": \"FABP1 transports fatty acids into the nucleus\", \"followingEvent\": [400143], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"FABP1 transports fatty acids into the nucleus\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2025-06-18\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2026996\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2026996.2\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-400143\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-400143.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 400148, \"displayName\": \"PPAR-alpha is activated by binding polyunsaturated fatty aci...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"PPAR-alpha is activated by binding polyunsaturated fatty acids especially those having 18-22 carbon groups and 2-6 double bonds such as linoleiate, linolenate, arachidonate, and eicosapentaenoate. These ligands bind the C-terminal region of PPAR-alpha. The fibrate drugs are also agonists of PPAR-alpha.<br>Binding of a ligand causes a conformational change in PPAR-alpha so that it recruits coactivators. By analogy with the closely related receptor PPAR-gamma, PPAR-alpha probably binds TBL1 and TBLR1, which are responsible for recruiting the 19S proteasome to degrade corepressors during the exchange of corepressors for coactivators. The coactivators belong to the CBP-SRC-HAT complex (CBP/p300, SRC1, SRC2, SRC3, CARM1, SWI/SNF, BAF60C, PRIC320, and PRIC285), the ASC complex (PRIP/ASC2, PIMT), and the TRAP-DRIP-ARC-MEDIATOR complex (TRAP130, PBP/TRAP220). The coactivators contain LXXLL motifs (Nuclear Receptor Boxes) that interact with the AF-2 region in nuclear receptors such as PPAR-alpha. Additionally bilirubin binds to PPAR-alpha and acts as coactivator.\"}]}" ;
