d\": 9842380, \"displayName\": \"(4E)-CERA [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"(4E)-CERA\", \"(4E)-unsatiated ceramide\"], \"producedByEvent\": [428259], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9842380\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9842380.1\"}, {\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 9842694, \"displayName\": \"CYB5B:Fe3+ [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"CYB5B:Fe3+\", \"ferric CYB5B\"], \"producedByEvent\": [428259, 428259], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9842694\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9842694.1\"}, 9842694], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 428185, \"displayName\": \"Ceramide synthases transfer acyl-CoA onto sphingoid\", \"followingEvent\": [428259], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ceramide synthases transfer acyl-CoA onto sphingoid\", \"sphingoid + acyl-CoA => dihydroceramide + CoASH\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-428185\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-428185.4\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821384, \"definition\": \"structure updated after externally and internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"two stars\", \"name\": [\"two stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-428259\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-428259.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 428244, \"displayName\": \"DEGS1 (DES1, sphingolipid delta(4)-desaturase 1 / “degenerat...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"DEGS1 (DES1, sphingolipid delta(4)-desaturase 1 / “degenerative spermatocyte homolog 1”) enzyme associated with the cytosolic face of the endoplasmic reticulum catalyzes the desaturation of dihydroceramide to form ceramide (Cadena et al. 1997; Ternes et al. 2002). The stoichiometry and cofactor requirements of the reaction are inferred from those observed in studies of ceramide synthesis in vitro catalyzed by rat liver microsomes (Michel et al. 1997). Apparently, DEGS1 is part of an enzyme complex, together with non-heme cytochrome b5 carrying Fe2+, that provides the reduction equivalent, which is subsequently refreshed by NADH (Geeraert et al., 1997; reviewed by Fabrias et al., 2011). The reaction is necessary as a step in ceramide biosynthesis, dihydroceramides and their downstream products like dihydrosphingomyelins are biologically active, for example, as part of lipid rafts, and inhibition of DEGS1 is a therapeutic target in cancer treatment (reviewed by Fabrias et al., 2011; Tzou et al., 2023). Mutations in DEGS1 cause hypomyelinating leukodystrophy (HLD18, MIM:618404) (reviewed by Wong et al., 2023).\"}]}" ;
