sine\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-428262\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-428262.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10144625, \"displayName\": \"ACER3 hydrolyzes phytoceramide\", \"inferredFrom\": [428262], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ACER3 hydrolyzes phytoceramide\", \"phytoceramide + H2O => fatty acid + phytosphingosine\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-428262\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-428262.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10021701, \"displayName\": \"ACER3 hydrolyzes phytoceramide\", \"inferredFrom\": [428262], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ACER3 hydrolyzes phytoceramide\", \"phytoceramide + H2O => fatty acid + phytosphingosine\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-428262\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-428262.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 428237, \"displayName\": \"phytosphingosine [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"phytosphingosine\", \"phytosphingosine(1+)\"], \"producedByEvent\": [428262], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-428237\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-428237.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1861754, \"displayName\": \"RCOO- [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"RCOO-\", \"fatty acid anion\", \"carboxylate\", \"carboxylic acid\"], \"producedByEvent\": [428262], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1861754\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1861754.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 428260, \"displayName\": \"DEGS2 oxygenates dihydroceramide\", \"followingEvent\": [428262], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"DEGS2 oxygenates dihydroceramide\", \"dihydroceramide + Fe2+ + H+ + O2 => phytoceramide + Fe3+ + H2O\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-428260\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-428260.5\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-428262\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-428262.6\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 428226, \"displayName\": \"ACER3 (alkaline ceramidase 3) catalyzes the hydrolysis of ph...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"ACER3 (alkaline ceramidase 3) catalyzes the hydrolysis of phytoceramide to yield a free fatty acid and phytosphingosine. The fully functional ACER3 has a Ca2+ and a Zn2+ ion bound (Vasiliauskaité-Brooks et al., 2018). ACER3 hydrolyses ceramides, dihydroceramides, and phytoceramides with long unsaturated acyl chains (Hu et al., 2010; Casasampere et al., 2015). ACER3 mRNA is widely expressed in the body, although most abundant in the placenta. Immunofluorescence studies of cultured cells over-expressing GFP-tagged protein suggest its localization to membranes of the endoplasmic reticulum (annotated here) and the Golgi apparatus (Mao et al. 2001). Deficiencies in ACER3 activity lead to a form of leukodystrophy (PLDECO, MIM:617762) (reviewed by Mao & Obeid, 2008; Parveen et al., 2019; Duarte et al., 2020; Dehnavi et al., 2021).\"}]}" ;
