26-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-428664\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-428664.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29372, \"displayName\": \"Pi [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Pi\", \"hydrogenphosphate\", \"Orthophosphate\", \"Phosphate\", \"Inorganic Phosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [428664], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29372\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29372.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 428682, \"displayName\": \"SPG [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SPG\", \"sphingoid base(1+)\", \"sphingosine\"], \"producedByEvent\": [428664], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-428682\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-428682.6\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 428273, \"displayName\": \"SPHK1 phosphorylates sphingoid\", \"followingEvent\": [428664], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SPHK1 phosphorylates sphingoid\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-428273\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-428273.5\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9695949, \"displayName\": \"SPHK2 phosphorylates sphingoid\", \"followingEvent\": [428664], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SPHK2 phosphorylates sphingoid\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9695949\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9695949.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-428664\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-428664.5\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 428683, \"displayName\": \"SGPP1 and 2 (sphingosine-1-phosphate phosphatase 1 and 2) en...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"SGPP1 and 2 (sphingosine-1-phosphate phosphatase 1 and 2) enzymes associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane catalyze the hydrolysis of cytosolic sphingosine 1-phosphate (S1P), dihydro-S1P, and phyto-S1P. to form sphinganine (dihydrosphingosine, phytosphingosine) and orthophosphate. Availability of sphingoids versus sphingoid-1-phosphates has direct influence on all processes involving ceramides (Johnson et al. 2003; Ogawa et al. 2003; Giussani et al., 2006).\"}]}" ;
