\"Positive regulation by 'POMC(138-176) [cytosol]'\", \"regulatedEntity\": [469659], \"schemaClass\": \"PositiveRegulation\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1449720\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1449720.1\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-469659\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-469659.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 469660, \"displayName\": \"The conversion of testosterone to the most potent androgen, ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"The conversion of testosterone to the most potent androgen, 5-alpha-dihydrotestosterone (DHTEST), is catalyzed by microsomal 5alpha-steroid reductase 1 (SRD5A1) (Andersson & Russell 1990). SRD5A1 is expressed in the prostate and other androgen target sites. Corticotropin (Adrenocorticotropic hormone, ACTH) acts through melanocortin receptor type 2 (MC2R) to stimulate steroidogenesis, increasing the production of androgens (McKenna et al. 1997).\"}]}" ;
