"R-HSA-548843\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-548843.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 548799, \"displayName\": \"Acyl-CoA synthetase long-chain family member 4 (ACSL4) assoc...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Acyl-CoA synthetase long-chain family member 4 (ACSL4) associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane catalyses the conjugation of arachidonate (AA) with CoA to form arachidonyl-CoA (AA-CoA) (Longo et al. 2003, Meloni et al. 2003). By similarity, ACSL3 can also preferentially conjugate CoA on to AA (Yao & Ye 2008). These enzymes are involved in the activation of long-chain fatty acids for both synthesis of cellular lipids, and degradation via beta-oxidation.\"}]}" ;
