lkylglycerol into fatty aldehyde and glycerol\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-5696119\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-5696119.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 5696116, \"displayName\": \"fatty aldehyde [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"fatty aldehyde\"], \"producedByEvent\": [5696119], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-5696116\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-5696116.2\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 76116, \"displayName\": \"Glycerol [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Glycerol\"], \"producedByEvent\": [5696119], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-76116\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-76116.2\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29356, \"displayName\": \"H2O [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H2O\", \"water\"], \"producedByEvent\": [5696119], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29356\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29356.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 1497857, \"displayName\": \"q-BH2 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"q-BH2\", \"L-erythro-7,8-dihydrobiopterin\", \"dihydrobiopterin\", \"7,8-dihydrobiopterin\"], \"producedByEvent\": [5696119], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-1497857\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-1497857.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2015-09-22\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-5696119\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-5696119.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 5696127, \"displayName\": \"Ether lipids (alkylglycerols, glyceryl ethers) are essential...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Ether lipids (alkylglycerols, glyceryl ethers) are essential components of brain membranes, protect the eye from cataract, mediate signalling processes and are required for spermatogenesis. Alkylglycerol monooxygenase (AGMO) is a tetrahydrobiopterin-dependent protein and is the only enzyme known to cleave the ether bond of alkylglycerols and lyso-alkylglycerol phospholipids into fatty aldehydes and glycerol derivatives (Watschinger et al. 2010).\"}]}" ;
