tus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2017-03-27\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-6809764\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-6809764.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 6809756, \"displayName\": \"MTMR2 forms a heterodimer with SBF1 (MTMR5), an enzymaticall...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"MTMR2 forms a heterodimer with SBF1 (MTMR5), an enzymatically inactive myotubularin family member. The interaction of MTMR2 and SBF1 involves coiled-coil domains of both proteins. SBF1 promotes perinuclear localization of MTMR2 (Kim et al. 2003), presumably to the endoplasmic reticulum(ER) membrane, as both proteins can localize to the ER membrane (Berger et al. 2003, Li et al. 2014).\"}]}" ;
