idises estradiol (EST17b) to estrone (E1)\", \"inferredFrom\": [6810594], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"HSD17B14 tetramer oxidises estradiol (EST17b) to estrone (E1)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-6810594\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-6810594.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 193066, \"displayName\": \"E1 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"E1\", \"estrone\"], \"producedByEvent\": [6810594], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-193066\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-193066.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29364, \"displayName\": \"NADPH [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADPH\", \"NADPH(4-)\", \"TPNH\"], \"producedByEvent\": [6810594], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29364\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29364.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 70106, \"displayName\": \"H+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H+\", \"hydron\", \"proton\"], \"producedByEvent\": [6810594], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-70106\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-70106.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 193143, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 hydroxylates TEST to EST17b\", \"followingEvent\": [6810594], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 hydroxylates TEST to EST17b\", \"Testosterone is converted to estradiol\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-193143\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-193143.3\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2016-03-23\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-6810594\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-6810594.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 6810601, \"displayName\": \"17-beta-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenases are primarily involved...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"17-beta-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenases are primarily involved in the metabolism of 17-hydroxysteroids and of other substrates such as fatty acids, prostaglandins and xenobiotics. The human DHRS10 gene encodes 17-beta-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase 14 (HSD17B14) which in tetrameric form can oxidise estradiol (E2) to estrone (E1) in vitro (Lukacik et al. 2007). It shows highest expression in brain, liver and placenta and has been shown to act as a protective factor in breast cancer (Sivik et al. 2012).\"}]}" ;
