idic acid\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-75883\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-75883.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10115637, \"displayName\": \"DHRS7B reduces GO3P to HXDG3P\", \"inferredFrom\": [75883], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"DHRS7B reduces GO3P to HXDG3P\", \"O-hexadecylglycerone phosphate + NADPH + H+ => 1-hexadecyl glycerol-3-phosphate + NADP+\", \"Conversion of acylated DHAP to lysophosphatidic acid\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-75883\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-75883.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9995999, \"displayName\": \"DHRS7B reduces GO3P to HXDG3P\", \"inferredFrom\": [75883], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"DHRS7B reduces GO3P to HXDG3P\", \"O-hexadecylglycerone phosphate + NADPH + H+ => 1-hexadecyl glycerol-3-phosphate + NADP+\", \"Conversion of acylated DHAP to lysophosphatidic acid\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-75883\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-75883.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 390422, \"displayName\": \"HXDG3P [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"HXDG3P\", \"1-hexadecyl-sn-glycerol 3-phosphate\", \"1-hexadecylglycerol-3-phosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [75883], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-390422\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-390422.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29366, \"displayName\": \"NADP+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADP+\", \"NADP(3-)\", \"NADP\", \"NADP(+)\", \"Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"beta-Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"TPN\", \"Triphosphopyridine nucleotide\"], \"producedByEvent\": [75883], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29366\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29366.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 390402, \"displayName\": \"Movement of O-hexadecylglycerone phosphate from the peroxisomal matrix to the cytosol\", \"followingEvent\": [75883], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Movement of O-hexadecylglycerone phosphate from the peroxisomal matrix to the cytosol\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-04-01\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-390402\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-390402.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2004-07-06\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-75883\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-75883.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 178557, \"displayName\": \"DHRS7B (Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 7B) cataly...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"DHRS7B (Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 7B) catalyzes the reaction of NADPH and GO3P (O-hexadecyldihydroxyacetone phosphate) to  form HXDG3P (1-hexadecyl glycerol-3-phosphate) and NADP+. The enzyme is associated with the outer face of the peroxisomal membrane; its substrates and products are thought to be cytosolic. The properties of the human enzyme are inferred from those of an activity purified from guinea pig liver (Datta et al. 1990). More recent studies of HXDG3P metabolism in cultured human cells in which DHRS7B activity was knocked down confirm the specificity of the human enzyme (Lodhi et al. 2012).\"}]}" ;
