n\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8848215\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8848215.5\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 8848223, \"displayName\": \"Three human enzymes, two mitochondrial and one cytosolic, ca...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Three human enzymes, two mitochondrial and one cytosolic, catalyze the interconversion of acetyl-CoA and acetoacetyl-CoA. The cytosolic form, acetyl-CoA acetyltransferase tetramer (ACAT2 tetramer) (Song et al. 1994), catalyses the condensation of two acetyl-CoA (Ac-CoA) molecules to form acetoacetyl-CoA (ACA-CoA). This is the first step in the biosynthesis of cholesterol (Fukao et al. 1997).\"}]}" ;
