\"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8849969\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8849969.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 8849965, \"displayName\": \"Characterization of human INPP5F (SAC2) identified that it i...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Characterization of human INPP5F (SAC2) identified that it is a 4-phosphatase with highest activity against PI(4,5)P2, PI(3,4)P2, and PI(3,4,5)P3, generating PI(5)P, PI(3)P and PI(3,5)P2 respectively  (Nakatsu et al. 2015, Hsu et al. 2015). Inpp5f -/-  mice have elevated level of PIP3 and exhibit accentuated cardiac hypertrophy as measured by heart size, myocyte size and gene expression (Zhu et al. 2009).\"}]}" ;
