7B2 oxidises estradiol (EST17b) to estrone (E1)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-8862137\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-8862137.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10205965, \"displayName\": \"HSD17B2 oxidises estradiol (EST17b) to estrone (E1)\", \"inferredFrom\": [8862137], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"HSD17B2 oxidises estradiol (EST17b) to estrone (E1)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-8862137\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-8862137.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10083030, \"displayName\": \"HSD17B2 oxidises estradiol (EST17b) to estrone (E1)\", \"inferredFrom\": [8862137], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"HSD17B2 oxidises estradiol (EST17b) to estrone (E1)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-8862137\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-8862137.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 193066, \"displayName\": \"E1 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"E1\", \"estrone\"], \"producedByEvent\": [8862137], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-193066\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-193066.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29364, \"displayName\": \"NADPH [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADPH\", \"NADPH(4-)\", \"TPNH\"], \"producedByEvent\": [8862137], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29364\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29364.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 70106, \"displayName\": \"H+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H+\", \"hydron\", \"proton\"], \"producedByEvent\": [8862137], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-70106\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-70106.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 193143, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 hydroxylates TEST to EST17b\", \"followingEvent\": [8862137], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 hydroxylates TEST to EST17b\", \"Testosterone is converted to estradiol\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2007-05-15\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-193143\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-193143.3\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2016-06-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8862137\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8862137.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 8862155, \"displayName\": \"Estradiol 17-beta-dehydrogenase 2 (HSD17B2) is a microsomal ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Estradiol 17-beta-dehydrogenase 2 (HSD17B2) is a microsomal enzyme expressed in osteoblastic cells (Wu et al. 1993, Dong et al. 1998). It catalyses the oxidation of highly active beta-estradiol (E2) and testosterone into the weaker 17-ketosteroids estrone (E1) and androstene-3,17-dione, respectively. Osteoporosis is a common, age-related disease characterised by a systemic impairment of bone mass, increasing bone fragility and fracture risk. A drop in E2 and testosterone levels, occurring with ageing, is the main factor driving the onset and progression of this disease. Potent inhibitors of HSD17B2 could be a novel treatment for this disease (Gargano et al. 2015).\"}]}" ;
