 false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PTPN13:PLEKHA1,2 bind PI(3,4)P2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-8870332\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-8870332.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 8870324, \"displayName\": \"PTPN13:PLEKHA1,2:PIP2 [plasma membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 4, \"name\": [\"PTPN13:PLEKHA1,2:PIP2\"], \"producedByEvent\": [8870332], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8870324\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8870324.1\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1675949, \"displayName\": \"PI(3,4,5)P3 is dephosphorylated to PI(3,4)P2 by INPP5[2] at the plasma membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [8870332], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI(3,4,5)P3 is dephosphorylated to PI(3,4)P2 by INPP5[2] at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1675949\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1675949.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1676109, \"displayName\": \"PI4P is phosphorylated to PI(3,4)P2 by PI3K3C[2] at the plasma membrane\", \"followingEvent\": [8870332], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PI4P is phosphorylated to PI(3,4)P2 by PI3K3C[2] at the plasma membrane\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1676109\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1676109.2\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2016-09-19\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8870332\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8870332.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 8870334, \"displayName\": \"Insulin sensitivity is critically dependent on the activity ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Insulin sensitivity is critically dependent on the activity of PI3K (phosphoinositide 3-kinase) and generation of the phosphatidylinositol 3,4, 5-triphosphate (PIP3,PtdIns(3,4,5)P(3)) second messenger. Increasing evidence suggests that one of the immediate breakdown products of PIP3, phosphatidylinositol 3,4-diphosphate (PIP2, PtdIns(3,4)P(2)), might also function as a signalling molecule by controlling a negative-feedback loop that down-regulates the insulin and PI3K network. The pleckstrin homology domain-containing family A members 1 and 2 (PLEKHA1 and PLEKHA2, aka TAPP1 and TAPP2 respectively) can both specifically bind PIP2. PLEKHA1 and 2 are constituitively bound to tyrosine-protein phosphatase non-receptor type 13 (PTPN13, aka PTPL1) via its first PDZ domain and this interaction keeps PLEKHA1 and 2 localised to the cytosol (Kimber et al. 2003). With increasing PIP2 levels, produced by PI3K activity on PIP3, PTPN13-bound PLEKHA1 and 2 translocate to the plasma membrane where they bind PIP2 (Marshall et al. 2002, Wullschleger et al. 2011).\"}]}" ;
