"507-11\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 12055623, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Structure of human phosphatidylcholine transfer protein in complex with its ligand\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12055623\", \"volume\": 9, \"year\": 2002}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 8873829, \"displayName\": \"PC-TP/StARD2: Of membranes and metabolism\", \"journal\": \"Trends Endocrinol. Metab.\", \"pages\": \"449-56\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 20338778, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"PC-TP/StARD2: Of membranes and metabolism\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20338778\", \"volume\": 21, \"year\": 2010}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 8873818, \"displayName\": \"Phosphatidylcholine transfer protein interacts with thioesterase superfamily member 2 to attenuate insulin signaling\", \"journal\": \"Sci Signal\", \"pages\": \"ra64\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 23901139, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Phosphatidylcholine transfer protein interacts with thioesterase superfamily member 2 to attenuate insulin signaling\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23901139\", \"volume\": 6, \"year\": 2013}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 8873815, \"displayName\": \"Thioesterase superfamily member 2 (Them2) and phosphatidylcholine transfer protein (PC-TP) interact to promote fatty acid oxidation and control glucose utilization\", \"journal\": \"Mol. Cell. Biol.\", \"pages\": \"2396-408\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 24732803, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Thioesterase superfamily member 2 (Them2) and phosphatidylcholine transfer protein (PC-TP) interact to promote fatty acid oxidation and control glucose utilization\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24732803\", \"volume\": 34, \"year\": 2014}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTP binds PC\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10815768, \"displayName\": \"PCTP binds PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTP binds PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Gallus gallus\", \"stId\": \"R-GGA-8873794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-GGA-8873794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10639260, \"displayName\": \"PCTP binds PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTP binds PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-8873794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-8873794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10543755, \"displayName\": \"PCTP binds PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTP binds PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-8873794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-8873794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10430036, \"displayName\": \"PCTP binds PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTP binds PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-8873794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-8873794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10316553, \"displayName\": \"PCTP binds PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTP binds PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-8873794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-8873794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10208086, \"displayName\": \"PCTP binds PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTP binds PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-8873794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-8873794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10085095, \"displayName\": \"PCTP binds PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTP binds PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-8873794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-8873794.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 8873866, \"displayName\": \"PCTP:PC [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"PCTP:PC\"], \"producedByEvent\": [8873794], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8873866\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8873866.1\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2016-09-19\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8873794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8873794.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 8873882, \"displayName\": \"Phosphatidylcholine transfer protein (PCTP aka STARD2) is a ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Phosphatidylcholine transfer protein (PCTP aka STARD2) is a member of the steroidogenic acute regulatory protein (StAR)-related lipid transfer (START) domain superfamily, a functionally diverse group of proteins that share a unique structural motif for binding lipids (the START domain). PCTP is widely expressed with highest expression levels in oxidative tissues, including liver, heart, muscle, kidney and brown fat but very little expression in white adipose tissue. PCTP exclusively binds phosphatidylcholine (PC) in the cytosol of cells and may mediate PC exchange at cellular membranes (Roderick et al. 2002). Recent mouse studies reveals a key regulatory role for PCTP in lipid and glucose metabolism. PCTP appears to limit access of fatty acids to mitochondria by binding to (Ersoy et al. 2013) and stimulating the activity of acyl-coenzyme A thioesterase 13 (ACOT13, aka Acyl-CoA thioesterase 13, THEM2), an enzyme that catalyses the hydrolysis of acyl-CoAs to their free fatty acids (Kawano et al. 2014). Ultimately, insulin signaling is downregulated (Kang et al. 2010).\"}]}" ;
