ng in Alveolar Type II Cells\", \"journal\": \"J. Biol. Chem.\", \"pages\": \"18559-74\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 26048993, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Lysophosphatidylcholine Acyltransferase 1 (LPCAT1) Specifically Interacts with Phospholipid Transfer Protein StarD10 to Facilitate Surfactant Phospholipid Trafficking in Alveolar Type II Cells\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/26048993\", \"volume\": 290, \"year\": 2015}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10722038, \"displayName\": \"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873923], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Xenopus tropicalis\", \"stId\": \"R-XTR-8873923\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-XTR-8873923.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10639274, \"displayName\": \"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873923], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-8873923\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-8873923.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10543778, \"displayName\": \"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873923], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-8873923\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-8873923.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10430059, \"displayName\": \"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873923], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-8873923\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-8873923.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10316576, \"displayName\": \"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873923], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-8873923\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-8873923.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10208109, \"displayName\": \"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873923], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-8873923\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-8873923.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10085118, \"displayName\": \"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\", \"inferredFrom\": [8873923], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"STARD10 binds LPCAT1 and PC\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-8873923\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-8873923.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 8873921, \"displayName\": \"STARD10:LPCAT1:PC [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"STARD10:LPCAT1:PC\"], \"producedByEvent\": [8873923], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8873921\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8873921.1\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1482547, \"displayName\": \"1-acyl LPC is acylated to PC by LPCAT\", \"followingEvent\": [8873923], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"1-acyl LPC is acylated to PC by LPCAT\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482547\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482547.2\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 1482533, \"displayName\": \"2-acyl LPC is acylated to PC by LPCAT\", \"followingEvent\": [8873923], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"2-acyl LPC is acylated to PC by LPCAT\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2012-06-12\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-1482533\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-1482533.2\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821385, \"definition\": \"structure upated after externally reviewed and then internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"four stars\", \"name\": [\"four stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"releaseDate\": \"2016-09-19\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8873923\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8873923.3\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 8873922, \"displayName\": \"The steroidogenic acute regulatory (StAR) protein-related li...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"The steroidogenic acute regulatory (StAR) protein-related lipid transfer (START) domain proteins constitute a family of evolutionarily conserved and widely expressed proteins that have been implicated in lipid transport, metabolism, and signaling. Human PCTP-like protein (STARD10) (Olayioye et al. 2005) is thought to be a dual specificity lipid transfer protein capable of shuttling phosphatidylcholine (PC) (and phosphatidylethanolamine (PE), not shown here) between intracellular membranes, especially to lamellar body membranes. Saturated PC is a major component of pulmonary surfactant, a mixture of proteins and phospholipids that plays an important role in facilitating gas exchange by maintaining alveolar stability. After synthesis in the endoplasmic reticulum, saturated PC is transported to lamellar bodies (LBs) for storage prior to secretion. Lysophosphatidylcholine acyltransferase 1 (LPCAT1) mediated reacylation is a final step in saturated PC synthesis prior to transport and LPCAT1 is proposed to form a complex with STARD10 at the ER membrane to facilitate the synthesis then transport of saturated PC to LBs (Lin et al. 2015).\"}]}" ;
