EPE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Gallus gallus\", \"stId\": \"R-GGA-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-GGA-9018880.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10727502, \"displayName\": \"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\", \"inferredFrom\": [9018880], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Xenopus tropicalis\", \"stId\": \"R-XTR-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-XTR-9018880.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10645061, \"displayName\": \"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\", \"inferredFrom\": [9018880], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-9018880.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10550885, \"displayName\": \"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\", \"inferredFrom\": [9018880], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-9018880.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10437462, \"displayName\": \"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\", \"inferredFrom\": [9018880], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-9018880.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10323574, \"displayName\": \"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\", \"inferredFrom\": [9018880], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-9018880.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10215690, \"displayName\": \"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\", \"inferredFrom\": [9018880], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-9018880.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10092465, \"displayName\": \"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\", \"inferredFrom\": [9018880], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises EPA to 18(R)-HpEPE or 18(S)-HpEPE\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-9018880.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Set\", \"dbId\": 9022921, \"displayName\": \"18(S)-HpEPE, 18(R)-HpEPE [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"18(S)-HpEPE, 18(R)-HpEPE\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9018880], \"schemaClass\": \"DefinedSet\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9022921\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9022921.1\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 2314686, \"displayName\": \"ASA- acetylates PTGS2\", \"followingEvent\": [9018880], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ASA- acetylates PTGS2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2011-12-06\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-2314686\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-2314686.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2018-03-21\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9018880\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9018880.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9020464, \"displayName\": \"Normally, cyclooxygenases (COX) carry out stereospecific oxy...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Normally, cyclooxygenases (COX) carry out stereospecific oxygenation of arachidonic acid to generate prostaglandins. When treated with aspirin (acetylsalicylic acid, ASA), dimeric cyclooxygenase 2 (COX2, PTGS2 dimer) can be acetylated. ASA covalently modifies PTGS2 by acetylating a serine residue at position 530 within the cyclooxygenase active site (Lucido et al. 2016). Acetylated PTGS2 dimer (Ac-PTGS2 dimer) changes the oxygenation stereospecificity towards its substrates, perhaps by steric shielding effects (Tosco 2013), producing a shift in lipid mediator production. Ac-PTGS2 dimer expressed in neutrophils can be acetylated by ASA, which now switches to mediate biosynthesis of precursors of endogenous antiinflammatory mediators. Ac-PTGS2 dimer is able to incorporate molecular oxygen into eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) to form the stereoisomers 18(S)- and 18(R)-hydroperoxy-eicosapentaenoic acid (18(S)- and 18(R)-HpEPE respectively) (Serhan et al. 2000, Oh et al. 2011).\"}]}" ;
