w.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23471029\", \"volume\": 54, \"year\": 2013}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9026002, \"displayName\": \"Total synthesis of neuroprotectin D1 analogues derived from omega-6 docosapentaenoic acid (DPA) and adrenic acid (AdA) from a common pivotal, late-stage intermediate\", \"journal\": \"J. Org. Chem.\", \"pages\": \"2657-65\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 24571431, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Total synthesis of neuroprotectin D1 analogues derived from omega-6 docosapentaenoic acid (DPA) and adrenic acid (AdA) from a common pivotal, late-stage intermediate\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24571431\", \"volume\": 79, \"year\": 2014}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 11051146, \"displayName\": \"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\", \"inferredFrom\": [9025152], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Dictyostelium discoideum\", \"stId\": \"R-DDI-9025152\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DDI-9025152.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10645299, \"displayName\": \"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\", \"inferredFrom\": [9025152], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-9025152\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-9025152.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10551183, \"displayName\": \"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\", \"inferredFrom\": [9025152], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-9025152\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-9025152.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10437774, \"displayName\": \"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\", \"inferredFrom\": [9025152], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-9025152\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-9025152.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10323894, \"displayName\": \"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\", \"inferredFrom\": [9025152], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-9025152\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-9025152.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10216003, \"displayName\": \"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\", \"inferredFrom\": [9025152], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-9025152\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-9025152.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10092791, \"displayName\": \"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\", \"inferredFrom\": [9025152], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX15 oxidises DPAn-6 to 17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-9025152\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-9025152.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Set\", \"dbId\": 9025151, \"displayName\": \"17(S)-HDPAn-6, 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"17(S)-HDPAn-6, 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9025152], \"schemaClass\": \"DefinedSet\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9025151\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9025151.1\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2018-03-21\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9025152\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9025152.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9025153, \"displayName\": \"Of the 5-, 12- and 15-lipoxygenases, 15-lipoxygenase is the ...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Of the 5-, 12- and 15-lipoxygenases, 15-lipoxygenase is the most efficient enzyme in oxygenating docosapentaenoic acids DPAn-6 and DPAn-3 as well as docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) at efficiencies 100%, 85% and 50% respectively. The main products of DPAn-6 oxygenation were found to be 17(S)-hydroxy-DPAn-6 and (10(S),17(S)-dihydroxy-DPAn-6 (17(S)-HDPAn-6 and 10(S),17(S)-diHDPAn-6 respectively) (Dangi et al. 2009, 2010, Dobson et al. 2013, Dayaker et al. 2014). Tested in two animal models of acute inflammation (Dangi et al. 2010) and human peripheral mononuclear cells (Nauroth et al. 2010), both compounds possessed potent anti-inflammatory activity. These DPAn-6 products are analogous in structure and action to DHA (docosahexaenoic acid)-derived resolvins (Dangi et al. 2010).\"}]}" ;
