el proresolving and tissue-regenerative resolvin and protectin sulfido-conjugated pathways\", \"journal\": \"FASEB J.\", \"pages\": \"2120-36\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 25713027, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Novel proresolving and tissue-regenerative resolvin and protectin sulfido-conjugated pathways\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25713027\", \"volume\": 29, \"year\": 2015}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"GGT hydrolyses PCTR2 to PCTR3\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 9026906, \"displayName\": \"PCTR3 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PCTR3\", \"16(S)-cystein-S-yl,17(R)-hydroxy-(4Z,7Z,10,12,14,19Z)-docosahexaenoate(1-)\", \"PCTR3(1-)\", \"16(S)-cystein-S-yl,17(R)-hydroxy-(4Z,7Z,10,12,14,19Z)-docosahexaenoic acid\", \"16-cysteinyl, 17-hydroxy-4Z,7Z,10,12,14,19Z-docosahexaenoic acid\", \"protectin conjugate in tissue regeneration 3\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9026907], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9026906\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9026906.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29424, \"displayName\": \"Gly [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Gly\", \"glycine zwitterion\", \"L-glycine\", \"glycine\", \"Aminoacetic acid\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9026907], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29424\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29424.6\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9026912, \"displayName\": \"GGT hydrolyses PCTR1 to PCTR2\", \"followingEvent\": [9026907], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"GGT hydrolyses PCTR1 to PCTR2\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2018-03-21\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9026912\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9026912.2\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2018-03-21\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9026907\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9026907.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9026904, \"displayName\": \"In human macrophages, protectin conjugate in tissue regenera...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"In human macrophages, protectin conjugate in tissue regeneration 3 (PCTR2) is proposed to be hydrolysed to PCTR3 (16-cysteinyl, 17-hydroxy-docosahexaenoic acid) by the actions of a glutathione transferase (GGT). Human macrophages incubated with E. coli and a GGT inhibitor led to increased levels of PCTR1 and decreased levels of PCTR3, suggesting a role for GGT enzyme in PCTR2 and PCTR3 biosynthesis (Dalli et al. 2015).\"}]}" ;
