 \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9027533, \"displayName\": \"Cyclooxygenase-2 generates anti-inflammatory mediators from omega-3 fatty acids\", \"journal\": \"Nat. Chem. Biol.\", \"pages\": \"433-41\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 20436486, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Cyclooxygenase-2 generates anti-inflammatory mediators from omega-3 fatty acids\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20436486\", \"volume\": 6, \"year\": 2010}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Dehydrogenase dehydrogenates 13(R)-HDPAn-3 to 13-oxo-DPAn-3\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 9027602, \"displayName\": \"13-oxo-DPAn-3 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"13-oxo-DPAn-3\", \"(7Z,10Z,14E,16Z,19Z)-13-oxodocosapentaenoate\", \"13-oxo-omega-3-docosapentaenoic acid\", \"(7Z,10Z,14E,16Z,19Z)-13-oxodocosapentaenoic acid\", \"EFOX-D5\", \"13-oxo-ω-3-docosapentaenoic acid\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9027598], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9027602\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9027602.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29364, \"displayName\": \"NADPH [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADPH\", \"NADPH(4-)\", \"TPNH\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9027598], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29364\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29364.4\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9026408, \"displayName\": \"PTGS2 dimer oxidises DPAn-3 to 13(R)-HDPAn-3\", \"followingEvent\": [9027598], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PTGS2 dimer oxidises DPAn-3 to 13(R)-HDPAn-3\", \"(7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-docosapentaenoate + AH2 + O2 => 13R-hydroxy-(7Z,10Z,14E,16Z,19Z)-docosapentaenoate + A + H2O\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2018-03-21\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9026408\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9026408.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2018-03-21\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9027598\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9027598.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9027606, \"displayName\": \"In activated macrophages, an unknown dehdyrogenase abstracts...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"In activated macrophages, an unknown dehdyrogenase abstracts hydrogen from 13-hydroxy-docosapentaenoic acid (13(R)-HDPAn-3) to form the electrophilic oxo (EFOX)derivative 13-oxo-DPAn-3 (Groeger et al. 2010). Potential candidates are cellular dehydrogenases such as 3α-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenases (3α-HSDs), which can convert 13- and 17-HDHA into corresponding EFOXs in the presence of NAD(P)+ <i>in vitro</i> (supplementary data, Groeger et al. 2010) or 5- and 15-hydroxyeicosanoid dehydrogenases (5- and 15-HEDH), which convert LOX products to 5-and 15-oxoETE (Erlemann et al. 2007). EFOXs can act as peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor-γ (PPARγ) agonists and inhibit pro-inflammatory cytokine and nitric oxide production, confirming their anti-inflammatory actions (Groeger et al. 2010).\"}]}" ;
