\"NADP+\", \"NADP(3-)\", \"NADP\", \"NADP(+)\", \"Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"beta-Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate\", \"TPN\", \"Triphosphopyridine nucleotide\"], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29366\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29366.5\"}], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"literatureReference\": [{\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9028212, \"displayName\": \"Generation and dietary modulation of anti-inflammatory electrophilic omega-3 fatty acid derivatives\", \"journal\": \"PLoS ONE\", \"pages\": \"e94836\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 24736647, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Generation and dietary modulation of anti-inflammatory electrophilic omega-3 fatty acid derivatives\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24736647\", \"volume\": 9, \"year\": 2014}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9023711, \"displayName\": \"Substrate selectivity of 5-hydroxyeicosanoid dehydrogenase and its inhibition by 5-hydroxy-Delta6-long-chain fatty acids\", \"journal\": \"J. Pharmacol. Exp. Ther.\", \"pages\": \"335-41\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 19164464, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Substrate selectivity of 5-hydroxyeicosanoid dehydrogenase and its inhibition by 5-hydroxy-Delta6-long-chain fatty acids\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19164464\", \"volume\": 329, \"year\": 2009}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"5-HEDH dehydrogenates 7-HDPAn-3 to 7-oxo-DPAn-3\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 9028200, \"displayName\": \"7-oxo-DPAn-3 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"7-oxo-DPAn-3\", \"(8E,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-7-oxodocosapentaenoate\", \"(8E,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-7-oxodocosapentaenoic acid\", \"7-oxo-omega3-docosapentaenoic acid\", \"7-oxo-ω-3-docosapentaenoic acid\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9027625], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9028200\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9028200.5\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 29364, \"displayName\": \"NADPH [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"NADPH\", \"NADPH(4-)\", \"TPNH\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9027625], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-29364\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-29364.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 70106, \"displayName\": \"H+ [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"H+\", \"hydron\", \"proton\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9027625], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-70106\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-70106.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9027633, \"displayName\": \"ALOX5 oxidises DPAn-3 to 7-HDPAn-3\", \"followingEvent\": [9027625], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ALOX5 oxidises DPAn-3 to 7-HDPAn-3\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2018-03-21\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9027633\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9027633.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2018-03-21\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9027625\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9027625.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9028198, \"displayName\": \"In neutrophils, 5-hydroxyeicosanoid dehydrogenase (5-HEDH) a...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"In neutrophils, 5-hydroxyeicosanoid dehydrogenase (5-HEDH) activity is localised in the microsomal fraction and requires NADP+ as a cofactor to oxidise 7-hydroxy-ω-3-docosapentaenoic acid (7-HDPAn-3) to 7-oxo-ω-3-docosapentaenoic acid (7-oxo-DPAn-3) (Patel et al. 2009, Cipollina et al. 2014). Although 5-HEDH activity has been found in a wide range of intact cells and in crude microsome preparations, the enzyme has not yet been purified, its structure is unknown, and the gene that encodes it remains to be identified. Dietary EPA supplementation significantly increases the formation of 7-oxo-DPAn-3 that transduces anti-inflammatory actions rather than suppressing production of pro-inflammatory AA metabolites (Cipollina et al. 2014).\"}]}" ;
