 \"volume\": 52, \"year\": 2014}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660202, \"displayName\": \"Comparative efficacy and safety of paricalcitol versus vitamin D receptor activators for dialysis patients with secondary hyperparathyroidism: a meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials\", \"journal\": \"BMC Nephrol\", \"pages\": \"272\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 28841848, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Comparative efficacy and safety of paricalcitol versus vitamin D receptor activators for dialysis patients with secondary hyperparathyroidism: a meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/28841848\", \"volume\": 18, \"year\": 2017}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660124, \"displayName\": \"Comparison between paricalcitol and active non-selective vitamin D receptor activator for secondary hyperparathyroidism in chronic kidney disease: a systematic review and meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials\", \"journal\": \"Int Urol Nephrol\", \"pages\": \"571-84\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 26748501, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Comparison between paricalcitol and active non-selective vitamin D receptor activator for secondary hyperparathyroidism in chronic kidney disease: a systematic review and meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/26748501\", \"volume\": 48, \"year\": 2016}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660193, \"displayName\": \"Comparison of oral falecalcitriol and intravenous calcitriol in hemodialysis patients with secondary hyperparathyroidism: a randomized, crossover trial\", \"journal\": \"Clin. Nephrol.\", \"pages\": \"660-8\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 19473635, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Comparison of oral falecalcitriol and intravenous calcitriol in hemodialysis patients with secondary hyperparathyroidism: a randomized, crossover trial\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19473635\", \"volume\": 71, \"year\": 2009}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660122, \"displayName\": \"Comparison of paricalcitol with maxacalcitol injection in Japanese hemodialysis patients with secondary hyperparathyroidism\", \"journal\": \"Ther Apher Dial\", \"pages\": \"225-34\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 25363733, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Comparison of paricalcitol with maxacalcitol injection in Japanese hemodialysis patients with secondary hyperparathyroidism\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25363733\", \"volume\": 19, \"year\": 2015}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660215, \"displayName\": \"Double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized, right-left study comparing calcipotriol monotherapy with a combined treatment of calcipotriol and diflucortolone valerate in chronic plaque psoriasis\", \"journal\": \"Acta Derm Venereol Suppl (Stockh)\", \"pages\": \"5-8\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 11234559, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized, right-left study comparing calcipotriol monotherapy with a combined treatment of calcipotriol and diflucortolone valerate in chronic plaque psoriasis\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11234559\", \"year\": 2000}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660118, \"displayName\": \"Eldecalcitol for the treatment of osteoporosis\", \"journal\": \"Clin Interv Aging\", \"pages\": \"1313-21\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 24101867, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Eldecalcitol for the treatment of osteoporosis\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24101867\", \"volume\": 8, \"year\": 2013}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660176, \"displayName\": \"Oral doxercalciferol therapy for secondary hyperparathyroidism in a peritoneal dialysis patient\", \"journal\": \"Clin. Nephrol.\", \"pages\": \"155-60\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 12227689, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Oral doxercalciferol therapy for secondary hyperparathyroidism in a peritoneal dialysis patient\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12227689\", \"volume\": 58, \"year\": 2002}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660175, \"displayName\": \"Osteoporosis treatment by a new active vitamin D3 compound, eldecalcitol, in Japan\", \"journal\": \"Curr Osteoporos Rep\", \"pages\": \"248-50\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 22918710, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Osteoporosis treatment by a new active vitamin D3 compound, eldecalcitol, in Japan\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/22918710\", \"volume\": 10, \"year\": 2012}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660195, \"displayName\": \"Proactive treatment with calcipotriol reduces recurrence of plaque psoriasis\", \"journal\": \"J. Dermatol.\", \"pages\": \"402-5\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 26434738, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Proactive treatment with calcipotriol reduces recurrence of plaque psoriasis\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/26434738\", \"volume\": 43, \"year\": 2016}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660205, \"displayName\": \"Research on kidney and mineral metabolism in Japan: past, present, and future\", \"journal\": \"Clin. Exp. Nephrol.\", \"pages\": \"4-8\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 28005175, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Research on kidney and mineral metabolism in Japan: past, present, and future\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/28005175\", \"volume\": 21, \"year\": 2017}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9660169, \"displayName\": \"Successful treatment of alopecia areata with topical calcipotriol\", \"journal\": \"Ann Dermatol\", \"pages\": \"341-4\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 22879719, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Successful treatment of alopecia areata with topical calcipotriol\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/22879719\", \"volume\": 24, \"year\": 2012}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10326048, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10996056, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10911750, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Drosophila melanogaster\", \"stId\": \"R-DME-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DME-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10824733, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Gallus gallus\", \"stId\": \"R-GGA-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-GGA-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10729407, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Xenopus tropicalis\", \"stId\": \"R-XTR-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-XTR-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10647016, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10553361, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10440039, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10218479, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-9660192.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10095173, \"displayName\": \"VDR agonists bind VDR\", \"inferredFrom\": [9660192], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"VDR agonists bind VDR\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-9660192.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 9660135, \"displayName\": \"VDR:VDR agonists [nucleoplasm]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 3, \"name\": [\"VDR:VDR agonists\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9660192], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9660135\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9660135.1\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2022-06-09\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9660192\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9660192.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9660143, \"displayName\": \"The genomic mechanism of 1,25(OH)2D action involves the dire...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"The genomic mechanism of 1,25(OH)2D action involves the direct, high-affinity binding of 1,25(OH)2D-activated VDR/RXRA to specific vitamin D response elements (VDREs) in and around target genes resulting in either activation or repression of transcription (Christakos et al. 2016). Vitamin D receptor (VDR) agonist drugs function in the same way as 1,25(OH)2D, resulting in activation of gene transcription. VDR agonist drugs bind VDR and activate transcription of genes involved in calcium and bone homeostasis and proliferation and differentiation. These drugs are used to treat secondary hyperparathyroidism (SHPT), bone diseases such as osteoporosis, psoriasis and alopecia.<br><br>Paricalcitol (trade name Zemplar) is a VDR agonist drug used for the prevention and treatment of secondary hyperparathyroidism, SHPT, causing excessive secretion of parathyroid hormone associated with chronic renal failure. It is an analog of 1,25-dihydroxyergocalciferol, the active form of vitamin D2 (ergocalciferol). However current evidence is not sufficient to demonstrate an advantage of paricalcitol over non-selective vitamin D derivatives for this indication (Cai et al. 2016, Xie et al. 2017). Doxercalciferol (trade name Hectorol) is a VDR agonist drug for secondary hyperparathyroidism and metabolic bone disease (Sprague & Ho 2002). It is a synthetic analog of ergocalciferol (vitamin D2). It suppresses parathyroid synthesis and secretion. Doxercalciferol needs a 25-hydroxylation step in the liver to become active and is independent of renal or extrarenal 1α-hydroxylase.<br><br>Eldecalcitol (trade name Edirol) is a VDR agonist drug used in Japan for the treatment of osteoporosis. Studies suggest Eldecalcitol reduces calcium reabsorption into the body from bones, therefore increasing bone mineral density, and increases calcium absorption in intestines (Matsumoto 2012, Noguchi et al. 2013). Calcipotriol (trade names Dovonex, Daivonex and Psorcutan) is a synthetic derivative of the active form of vitamin D, calcitriol. It is used in the long-term treatment of chronic plaque psoriasis (Salmhofer et al. 2000, Ito et al. 2016) and alopecia areata (Kim et al. 2012). Falecalcitriol (Ito et al. 2009) and maxacalcitol (Akizawa et al. 2015) are used to treat SHPT in Japan (Honda et al. 2014, Mizobuchi et al. 2017).\"}]}" ;
