transport S1P from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"inferredFrom\": [9695890], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SPNS2,MFSD2B transport S1P from cytosol to extracellular region\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-9695890\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-9695890.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10219194, \"displayName\": \"SPNS2,MFSD2B transport S1P from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"inferredFrom\": [9695890], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SPNS2,MFSD2B transport S1P from cytosol to extracellular region\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-9695890\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-9695890.1\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10095922, \"displayName\": \"SPNS2,MFSD2B transport S1P from cytosol to extracellular region\", \"inferredFrom\": [9695890], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SPNS2,MFSD2B transport S1P from cytosol to extracellular region\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-9695890\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-9695890.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 9843733, \"displayName\": \"S1P [extracellular region]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"S1P\", \"sphingoid 1-phosphate(1-)\", \"sphingoid 1-phosphate\", \"phys-ent-participant40241\", \"phys-ent-participant40259\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9695890], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9843733\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9843733.2\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 428273, \"displayName\": \"SPHK1 phosphorylates sphingoid\", \"followingEvent\": [9695890], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SPHK1 phosphorylates sphingoid\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-428273\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-428273.5\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9695949, \"displayName\": \"SPHK2 phosphorylates sphingoid\", \"followingEvent\": [9695890], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SPHK2 phosphorylates sphingoid\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2009-09-30\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9695949\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9695949.4\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2020-09-15\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9695890\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9695890.4\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9695893, \"displayName\": \"Several different transporters catalyze the secretion of sph...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Several different transporters catalyze the secretion of sphingosine 1-phosphate (S1P). S1P is a signaling molecule that regulates many physiological processes in development and the immune system. S1P is produced inside cells, so it must be secreted to exert its effects through its receptors. Protein spinster homolog 2 (SPNS2) is an S1P transporter involved in S1P secretion and regulation of its levels in the lymph, thereby playing a role in lymphocyte trafficking (Nagahashi et al., 2013; Chen et al., 2023; reviewed by Spiegel et al., 2019). MFSD2A exports S1P and is mainly expressed in erythrocytes and platelets, having the function, together with SPNS2, of maintaining the blood-brain barrier (Kobayashi et al., 2018; reviewed by Ghaderi & Levkau, 2023). There is evidence in rats of S1P export by rat homologs of ABCA1, ABCA7, and ABCC1 (reviewed by Reitsema et al., 2014).\"}]}" ;
