ty is potently inhibited by finasteride and dutasteride\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25961201\", \"volume\": 2, \"year\": 2010}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9705795, \"displayName\": \"Dutasteride: a review of its use in the management of prostate disorders\", \"journal\": \"Drugs\", \"pages\": \"463-85\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 18318566, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Dutasteride: a review of its use in the management of prostate disorders\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18318566\", \"volume\": 68, \"year\": 2008}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9705810, \"displayName\": \"Finasteride for benign prostatic hyperplasia\", \"journal\": \"Am Fam Physician\", \"pages\": \"1511-4\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 1279965, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Finasteride for benign prostatic hyperplasia\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1279965\", \"volume\": 46, \"year\": 1992}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9705792, \"displayName\": \"An overview on 5alpha-reductase inhibitors\", \"journal\": \"Steroids\", \"pages\": \"109-53\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 19879888, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"An overview on 5alpha-reductase inhibitors\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19879888\", \"volume\": 75, \"year\": 2010}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9705769, \"displayName\": \"Inhibition of 5 alpha-reductase activity in human skin by zinc and azelaic acid\", \"journal\": \"Br J Dermatol\", \"pages\": \"627-32\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 3207614, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Inhibition of 5 alpha-reductase activity in human skin by zinc and azelaic acid\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/3207614\", \"volume\": 119, \"year\": 1988}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9705800, \"displayName\": \"Azelaic acid. A review of its pharmacological properties and therapeutic efficacy in acne and hyperpigmentary skin disorders\", \"journal\": \"Drugs\", \"pages\": \"780-98\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 1712709, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Azelaic acid. A review of its pharmacological properties and therapeutic efficacy in acne and hyperpigmentary skin disorders\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1712709\", \"volume\": 41, \"year\": 1991}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9705763, \"displayName\": \"[Mechanism of azelaic acid action in acne]\", \"journal\": \"G Ital Dermatol Venereol\", \"pages\": \"455-63\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 2534550, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"[Mechanism of azelaic acid action in acne]\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2534550\", \"volume\": 124, \"year\": 1989}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10996531, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9705794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-9705794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10825622, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9705794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Gallus gallus\", \"stId\": \"R-GGA-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-GGA-9705794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10730120, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9705794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Xenopus tropicalis\", \"stId\": \"R-XTR-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-XTR-9705794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10647721, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9705794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-9705794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10441112, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9705794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-9705794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10327050, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9705794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-9705794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10219562, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9705794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-9705794.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10096282, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9705794], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2 binds SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-9705794.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 9705766, \"displayName\": \"SRD5A2:SRD5A2 inhibitors [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 3, \"name\": [\"SRD5A2:SRD5A2 inhibitors\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9705794], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9705766\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9705766.1\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2022-06-09\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9705794\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9705794.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9705813, \"displayName\": \"The conversion of testosterone (TEST) to the most potent and...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"The conversion of testosterone (TEST) to the most potent androgen, 5-alpha-dihydrotestosterone (DHTEST), is catalyzed by microsomal 5alpha-steroid reductases 1-3 (SRD5A1-3). SRD5As are highly expressed in the prostate, the skin, and other androgen target sites. Benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH) is a pathologic process that can lead to the development of lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS) in men. BPH refers to stromal and glandular epithelial hyperplasia that occurs in the zone of the prostate that surrounds the urethra. This overgrowth is dependent mainly on androgens, particularly DHTEST. Since SRD5As are responsible for the production of DHTEST, SRD5A inhibitors can be used in the  treatment of symptomatic BPH (Rasmusson et al. 1986, Gisleskog et al. 1998).<br><br>The azasteroids finasteride and dutasteride are approved for human use to treat BPH (Sandhu 2009). Dutasteride can block all three SRD5A isoforms and can decrease DHTEST levels in the blood by up to 98% (Keam & Scott 2008, Yamana et al. 2010). In contrast, finasteride (Hasinki et al. 1992) only inhibits type II and III isoenzymes so is able to achieve a reduction in circulating DHTEST of only 65 to 70% (Yamana et al. 2010, Aggarwal et al. 2010). However, these two drugs decrease DHTEST levels in the prostate gland to a similar level, where the SRD5A2 isoform predominates.<br><br>The dicarboxylic acid azelaic acid is a potent inhibitor of SRD5A in human skin and could be an effective agent in the treatment of androgen related pathology of human skin such as various types of acne and cutaneous hyperpigmentary disorders (Stamatiadis et al. 1998, Fitton & Goa 1991, Passi et al. 1989). Its exact mechanism is unknown.\"}]}" ;
