cetoxy-4-androstene-3,17-dione and sustained effects in vivo\", \"journal\": \"Steroids\", \"pages\": \"693-702\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 7336466, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Inactivation of aromatase in vitro by 4-hydroxy-4-androstene-3,17-dione and 4-acetoxy-4-androstene-3,17-dione and sustained effects in vivo\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7336466\", \"volume\": 38, \"year\": 1981}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9707360, \"displayName\": \"Highly selective inhibition of estrogen biosynthesis by CGS 20267, a new non-steroidal aromatase inhibitor\", \"journal\": \"J Steroid Biochem Mol Biol\", \"pages\": \"1021-7\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 2149502, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Highly selective inhibition of estrogen biosynthesis by CGS 20267, a new non-steroidal aromatase inhibitor\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/2149502\", \"volume\": 37, \"year\": 1990}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9707318, \"displayName\": \"Approval summary: letrozole in the treatment of postmenopausal women with advanced breast cancer\", \"journal\": \"Clin Cancer Res\", \"pages\": \"665-9\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 11895893, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Approval summary: letrozole in the treatment of postmenopausal women with advanced breast cancer\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11895893\", \"volume\": 8, \"year\": 2002}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9707346, \"displayName\": \"An overview of the pharmacology and pharmacokinetics of the newer generation aromatase inhibitors anastrozole, letrozole, and exemestane\", \"journal\": \"Cancer\", \"pages\": \"2006-16\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 12404296, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"An overview of the pharmacology and pharmacokinetics of the newer generation aromatase inhibitors anastrozole, letrozole, and exemestane\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12404296\", \"volume\": 95, \"year\": 2002}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9707354, \"displayName\": \"HPMA copolymer-aminoglutethimide conjugates inhibit aromatase in MCF-7 cell lines\", \"journal\": \"J Drug Target\", \"pages\": \"459-70\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 16332571, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"HPMA copolymer-aminoglutethimide conjugates inhibit aromatase in MCF-7 cell lines\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16332571\", \"volume\": 13, \"year\": 2005}, {\"className\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"dbId\": 9707355, \"displayName\": \"Fadrozole hydrochloride: a potent, selective, nonsteroidal inhibitor of aromatase for the treatment of estrogen-dependent disease\", \"journal\": \"J Med Chem\", \"pages\": \"725-36\", \"pubMedIdentifier\": 1825337, \"schemaClass\": \"LiteratureReference\", \"title\": \"Fadrozole hydrochloride: a potent, selective, nonsteroidal inhibitor of aromatase for the treatment of estrogen-dependent disease\", \"url\": \"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1825337\", \"volume\": 34, \"year\": 1991}], \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"orthologousEvent\": [{\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10996535, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Caenorhabditis elegans\", \"stId\": \"R-CEL-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CEL-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10912317, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Drosophila melanogaster\", \"stId\": \"R-DME-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DME-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10825668, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Gallus gallus\", \"stId\": \"R-GGA-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-GGA-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10730226, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Xenopus tropicalis\", \"stId\": \"R-XTR-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-XTR-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10647767, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10554538, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Sus scrofa\", \"stId\": \"R-SSC-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-SSC-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10441259, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Bos taurus\", \"stId\": \"R-BTA-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-BTA-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10327193, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10219614, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-9707353.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10096429, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\", \"inferredFrom\": [9707353], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1 binds Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-9707353.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 9707321, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1:Aromatase inhibitors [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 3, \"name\": [\"CYP19A1:Aromatase inhibitors\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9707353], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9707321\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9707321.1\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2022-06-09\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9707353\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9707353.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9707323, \"displayName\": \"CYP19A1 (aromatase) is the enzyme that catalyses a key aroma...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"CYP19A1 (aromatase) is the enzyme that catalyses a key aromatization step in the synthesis of estrogens from androgens. Aromatase inhibitors work by inhibiting the action of the enzyme aromatase (Brodie et al. 1981). Many breast cancers are hormone receptor-positive, meaning their growth is stimulated and/or maintained by the presence of hormones such as estrogen or progesterone. In postmenopausal women, estrogen is primarily derived from the aromatization of adrenally-produced androgens into estrogens by CYP19A1. Aromatase inhibitors are a class of drugs used in the treatment of breast cancer in postmenopausal women by competitively inhibiting CYP19A1. As breast tissue is stimulated by estrogens, decreasing their production is a way of suppressing growth of hormone receptor-positive breast tumours (Chumsri et al. 2011). Aromatase inhibitors can be first-generation (e.g. aminoglutethimide) (Greco et al. 2005), second-generation (e.g. fadrozole) (Browne et al. 1991), and third-generation (e.g. anastrozole, letrozole, and exemestane) (Bhatnagar et al. 1990, Cohen et al. 2002, Buzdar et al. 2002) agents. They can also be divided into type I and type II inhibitors. Type I inhibitors have a steroidal structure similar to androgens and inactivate CYP19A1 irreversibly by blocking the substrate-binding site, and are therefore known as aromatase inactivators. Type II inhibitors are nonsteroidal and their action is reversible.\"}]}" ;
