"PSAP(195-273) forms a dimer\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-9840488\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-9840488.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10223660, \"displayName\": \"PSAP(195-273) forms a dimer\", \"inferredFrom\": [9840488], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PSAP(195-273) forms a dimer\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Rattus norvegicus\", \"stId\": \"R-RNO-9840488\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-RNO-9840488.1\"}, {\"category\": \"binding\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10100279, \"displayName\": \"PSAP(195-273) forms a dimer\", \"inferredFrom\": [9840488], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PSAP(195-273) forms a dimer\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Mus musculus\", \"stId\": \"R-MMU-9840488\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-MMU-9840488.1\"}], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Complex\", \"dbId\": 9840482, \"displayName\": \"PSAP(195-273) dimer [lysosomal lumen]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"isChimeric\": false, \"maxDepth\": 2, \"name\": [\"PSAP(195-273) dimer\", \"Sap B dimer\"], \"producedByEvent\": [9840488], \"schemaClass\": \"Complex\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9840482\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840482.1\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 9840334, \"displayName\": \"PSAP is cleaved\", \"followingEvent\": [9840488], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"PSAP is cleaved\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2023-09-13\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9840334\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840334.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2023-09-13\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9840488\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840488.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9840495, \"displayName\": \"Saposin B (PSAP(195-273)) is the only PSAP fragment that for...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Saposin B (PSAP(195-273)) is the only PSAP fragment that forms a dimer. The dimer is disulfide-linked and can switch between two conformations, one of which shows an open hydrophobic pocket, supporting a lipid solubilization mechanism for saposin B, consistent with the observation that saposin B can act as a lipid-transport protein (Vaccaro et al., 1995; Ahn et al., 2002; Ahn et al., 2003).\"}]}" ;
