 \"R-HSA-9840795\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840795.3\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2023-09-13\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9840833\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9840833.2\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9840836, \"displayName\": \"Ganglioside GA2 (asialo-GM2, ganglio-N-triaosylceramide), bo...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Ganglioside GA2 (asialo-GM2, ganglio-N-triaosylceramide), bound to GM2A, gets cleaved by the beta-hexosaminidase complexes A and B. It is present at elevated levels in nerve cells in Sandhoff disease (Tay-Sachs disease variant O, MIM: 268800), a hexosaminidase beta subunit (HEXB) deficiency, which leads to low levels of both bHEX complexes bHEXA and bHEXB (Sandhoff et al., 1971; reviewed in Sandhoff et al., 2018; Sandhoff & Sandhoff, 2018).\"}]}" ;
