eferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-201034\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-201034.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"omitted\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 8949399, \"displayName\": \"CAR translocates from the cytosol to the mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"followingEvent\": [9911362], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"CAR translocates from the cytosol to the mitochondrial intermembrane space\", \"(R)-carnitine(in) = (R)-carnitine(out)\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2017-03-27\", \"schemaClass\": \"BlackBoxEvent\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-8949399\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-8949399.3\"}, {\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 434382, \"displayName\": \"ACSL3,4 ligates coenzyme A (CoA-SH) to a long chain fatty acid yielding fatty acyl-coenzyme A\", \"followingEvent\": [9911362], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"ACSL3,4 ligates coenzyme A (CoA-SH) to a long chain fatty acid yielding fatty acyl-coenzyme A\", \"a long-chain fatty acid + ATP + CoA => a long-chain fatty acyl-CoA + AMP + diphosphate\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2019-03-20\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-434382\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-434382.4\"}, {\"category\": \"dissociation\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 5634100, \"displayName\": \"FABP5 dissociates from RXRA:PPARD:atRA\", \"followingEvent\": [9911362], \"isChimeric\": false, \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"FABP5 dissociates from RXRA:PPARD:atRA\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2014-12-11\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-5634100\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-5634100.2\"}], \"previousReviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821383, \"definition\": \"internally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"three stars\", \"name\": [\"three stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"regulatedBy\": [{\"className\": \"NegativeRegulation\", \"dbId\": 200418, \"displayName\": \"Negative regulation by 'Mal-CoA [cytosol]'\", \"regulatedEntity\": [9911362], \"schemaClass\": \"NegativeRegulation\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-200418\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-200418.3\"}], \"regulationReference\": [{\"className\": \"RegulationReference\", \"dbId\": 9642880, \"displayName\": \"Negative regulation by 'Mal-CoA [cytosol]' Structural model of a malonyl-CoA-binding site of carnitine octanoyltransferase and carnitine palmitoyltransferase I: mutational analysis of a malonyl-CoA affinity domain\", \"schemaClass\": \"RegulationReference\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2024-09-11\", \"reviewStatus\": {\"className\": \"ReviewStatus\", \"dbId\": 9821382, \"definition\": \"externally reviewed\", \"displayName\": \"five stars\", \"name\": [\"five stars\"], \"schemaClass\": \"ReviewStatus\"}, \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"HSA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 48887, \"displayName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"name\": [\"Homo sapiens\", \"H. sapiens\", \"Hs\", \"human\", \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9911362\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9911362.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9911368, \"displayName\": \"Carnitine palmitoyl transferase 1B (CPT1B) associated with t...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Carnitine palmitoyl transferase 1B (CPT1B) associated with the inner mitochondrial membrane, catalyzes the reaction of palmitoyl-CoA (PALM-CoA) from the cytosol with carnitine (CAR) in the mitochondrial intermembrane space to form palmitoylcarnitine (L-PCARN) and CoA-SH. Three CPT1 isoforms exist; CPT1A, B and C. In the body, CPT1A is most abundant in liver while CPT1B is abundant in muscle. CPT1C is mainly expressed in neurons and localises to the ER and not to the mitochondria. It has little or no enzymatic activity in fatty acid oxidation. Both CPT1A and CPT1B are inhibited by malonyl-CoA (Morillas et al. 2002, 2004; Zammit et al. 2001; Zhu et al. 1997).\"}]}" ;
