, \"man\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9606\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9915971\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9915971.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9915988, \"displayName\": \"Several cytochrome P450s (CYPs) convert arachidonate to 11,1...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"Several cytochrome P450s (CYPs) convert arachidonate to 11,12-epoxyeicosatrienoate (1,12-EET).  The CYPs and their references are: CYP1A1, CYP1A2, CYP1B1 (Choudhary et al. 2004); CYP2C8, CYP2C9 (Rifkind et al. 1995); CYP2C19 (Bylund et al. 1998, Rifkind et al. 1995); CYP2J2 (Wu et al. 1996).\"}]}" ;
