speciesName\": \"Homo sapiens\", \"stId\": \"R-HSA-9947203\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-HSA-9947203.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9947208, \"displayName\": \"MSMO1 (Methylsterol monooxygenase 1), associated with the en...\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"MSMO1 (Methylsterol monooxygenase 1), associated with the endoplasmic reticulum membrane, oxidizes 4,4-diMe5-cholest-8-en-3-ol to 4a-carboxy-4b-me-5a-cholest-8-en-3beta-ol. Evidence for this function of human MSMO1 protein is indirect, coming from studies of steroid synthesis intermediates accumulated in patients with defects in the enzyme (He et al. 2011).\"}]}" ;
